{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MF3JRevLKuv33hTs2JgzWh","type":"tool_result","content":"170: * HOW IT WORKS: E.Mode7 (the mode7 module) draws the floor, the sky and the karts far to near; E.Car and E.Race (the\n214:  const m7 = new E.Mode7({ floor: look, size: [SIZE, SIZE], outside: '#3c7a34', sky: new E.Backdrop('day'), far: 1400 });\n273:    players.forEach((R, i) => { const c = cams[i], k = 1 - Math.exp(-dt * 5); c.angle += E.angDiff(c.angle, R.car.angle) * k; m7.cam = c; m7.chase({ x: R.car.x, y: R.car.y, angle: c.angle }, { back: tall ? 74 : 42, h: (tall ? 38 : 24) + R.car.z * .5 }); c.\n295:    const v = m7.view(k), car = R.car, a = car.angle + (car.spinT > 0 ? 0 : car.drifting * .35), ground = m7.project(car.x, car.y, 0), dx = v.dx, dy = v.dy;\n305:  function trees(c) { const fx = Math.cos(c.angle), fy = Math.sin(c.angle); for (const [x, y] of TREES) { const d = (x - c.x) * fx + (y - c.y) * fy; if (d > 40 && d < 900) m7.sprite(TREE, x, y, 0, { scale: 1.6 }); } }\n309:      const p = LINE.at(t * 40); m7.cam = { x: p.x, y: p.y, h: 60, angle: p.angle, pitch: 14, fov: 70 }; trees(m7.cam);\n310:      m7.draw(r);\n320:    for (const R of race.racers) m7.add(R.car.x, R.car.y, R.car.z, (g, sx, sy, k) => drawKart(g, sx, sy, k, R));\n321:    for (const b of race.boxes) if (b.t <= 0) m7.add(b.x, b.y, 6 + Math.sin(t * 4) * 1.5, (g, sx, sy, k) => { const s = 7 * k, hue = (t * 120 + b.x) % 360; E.px.rect(g, sx - s, sy - s * 2, s * 2, s * 2, E.hsl(hue, .8, .55)); E.px.rect(g, sx - s + 1, sy - s\n322:    for (const s of race.shots) m7.add(s.x, s.y, 2, (g, sx, sy, k) => { E.px.disc(g, sx, sy - 3 * k, 4 * k, '#2a9a2a'); E.px.disc(g, sx - k, sy - 4 * k, 2 * k, '#8af08a'); });\n323:    for (const h of race.hazards) m7.add(h.x, h.y, 0, (g, sx, sy, k) => { E.px.poly(g, [[sx - 5 * k, sy], [sx, sy - 6 * k], [sx + 5 * k, sy], [sx, sy - 2 * k]], '#f0d030'); });\n324:    m7.draw(r, cam);\n----\n97:- 1512 Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js); E.Mode7: mode7\n1514:- `new E.Mode7(o = {}) → mode7`: new E.Mode7({ floor, size, outside, wrap, sky, fog, far }): a Mode 7 view (the manual above)\n---\n100:- 1596 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n1598:- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\n1599:- `road.add(n, o = {})`: n segments more, bending (curve) and climbing (hill: units up, - down), eased in and out; o.tunnel, o.colors\n1601:- `road.curveAt(z)`: how hard the road bends at a distance\n1602:- `road.draw(r, v = {})`: draw the road over r's frame (an overlay; r.viewport's part in a split screen): { z, x, h, turn, cars }\n1604:- `road.place(z, offset, what, scale = 8)`: scenery at distance z, offset across: what = an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or { draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w }\n1605:- `road.project(z, x, y = 0)`: a point (distance z, across x in half roads, height y over the road) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera last drawn, or null behind it\n1606:- `road.seg(z)`: the segment at a distance (it wraps)\n1611:- `road.segs = []`: its segments ({ i, z, y0, y1, curve, tunnel, colors, things })\n---\n99:- 1564 Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js); E.Rhythm: rhythm\n1566:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"26e2ef96-40e5-4193-9511-2f9a6b8fb5ef","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:11:41.764Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"170: * HOW IT WORKS: E.Mode7 (the mode7 module) draws the floor, the 