{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01425XSAgNtFxkavLgWb6tw7","type":"tool_result","content":"98:- 1535 Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js); E.Physics: physics\n1537:- `new E.Physics(o = {}) → physics`: new E.Physics({ gravity, substeps, iterations, sleep, on, cell }): a world of bodies (see the manual)\n---\n30:game.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\n276:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /). A preset's own halves c\n283:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(inpu\n293:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n296:- `input.mouseScreen()`: mouse position in projected screen pixels, or null\n297:- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n300:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n309:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n322:- `input.value(a)` †: how far action a is pressed, 0 to 1: a gamepad button by its travel (the triggers, even short of a press), a stick's direction (PadAxisUp ..., or up / down / left / right on the touch stick) by its push, any other code held 1\n332:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n334:- `input.mouse`: { cx, cy } its page position, active once it has moved over the canvas, t the input clock when it last moved\n343:- `input.padValues = []` †: each gamepad button's travel, 0 to 1 (the triggers; input.value reads them)\n345:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n430:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's\n476:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n479:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n499:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n500:- `game.removePlayer(p)` †: a player leaves (its input, or its number, 2 to 4); player 1 has the whole keyboard back when no one shares it\n527:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the ca\n569:- `E.PLAYER_COLORS: #4a8aff, #ff4a4a, #4ad860, #ffd040` †: the players' colors: player 1 blue, 2 red, 3 green, 4 yellow (game.players)\n777:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game who\n---\n55:- 220 Views (projections); E.View: view\n59:- 368 Lighting; game.lights\n224:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n370:- `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity = 1, o)` †: radius in world units; intensity ~0.5..1.5. opts: { color: '#ffaa55' (both lightings), shadow: true (GPU lighting: walls and casters block it) }\n371:- `game.lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` †: something that blocks light (GPU shadows): a cylinder of radius r from the floor up to height top\n372:- `game.lights.heat(x, y, z, width, strength = 1)` †: heat shimmer above a point (GPU only). width in world units, strength ~0.5..1.5\n373:- `game.lights.on` †: true when the canvas lighting draws this frame: enabled, or standing in for GPU lighting the game turned on that can't draw (no WebGPU, still loading, a side view); gpu.fallback = false keeps such a frame unlit\n374:- `game.lights.refresh()` †: rebuild the darkness bands after changing dark, levels or glow (lights.dark = [r, g, b]; lights.refresh())\n375:- `game.lights.render(r)` †: darken the frame by the lights (the renderer calls it after the queue, when enabled)\n376:- `game.lights.ambient = .15` †: how lit unlit places are, 0 (black) .. 1\n377:- `game.lights.dark = [10, 6, 24]` †: the color of darkness, [r, g, b]\n378:- `game.lights.darkness = .9` †: how dark the darkest places get, 0..1 (the smooth style, E.style.trans 'alpha')\n379:- `game.lights.enabled = false` †: false (the default) turns the canvas lighting off\n380:- `game.lights.glow = [255, 200, 140, 0]` †: the color, [r, g, b, a], where light is brightest\n381:- `game.lights.glowAt = 1.7` †: the light level (1 = fully lit) above which it glows\n382:- `game.lights.levels = [.9, .7, .48, .26, .08, 0]` †: the darkness of each lighting band, darkest first (dithered between them)\n383:- `game.lights.list = []` †: this frame's lights from add()\n384:- `game.lights.screen = false` †: true measures lights on the screen, not the ground (side views and PlatformMaps do it by themselves)\n385:- `game.lights.tint = .32` †: how strongly lights add their own color, 0..1\n432:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a wa\n436:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written),\n481:- `game.cornerArea()` †: where the corner's buttons (menu and full screen, top right; the touch START) cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (r.W and r.H's space), or null while none show: keep a HUD clear of it\n483:- `game.enableGPU(o = {})` †: turn on WebGPU lighting: where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with its own ambient (game.lights.ambient) and the same lights. opts: { map, bands, ambient, fallback, ..\n504:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n540:- `game.lights` †: canvas lighting (lights.enabled, lights.add in draw)\n627:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n628:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n629:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n630:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n631:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"524cbf4f-6343-4a38-8c8d-832b18cedcfa","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:11:44.333Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"98:- 1535 Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js); E.Physics: physics\n1537:- `new E.Physics(o = {}) → physics`: new E.Physics({ gravity, substeps, iterations, sleep, on, cell }): a world of bodies (see the manual)\n---\n30:game.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\n276:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /). A preset's own halves c\n283:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(inpu\n293:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n296:- `input.mouseScreen()`: mouse position in projected screen pixels, or null\n297:- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n300:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n309:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n322:- `input.value(a)` †: how far action a is pressed, 0 to 1: a gamepad button by its travel (the triggers, even short of a press), a stick's direction (PadAxisUp ..., or up / down / left / right on the touch stick) by its push, any other code held 1\n332:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n334:- `input.mouse`: { cx, cy } its page position, active once it has moved over the canvas, t the input clock when it last moved\n343:- `input.padValues = []` †: each gamepad button's travel, 0 to 1 (the triggers; input.value reads them)\n345:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n430:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's\n476:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n479:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n499:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n500:- `game.removePlayer(p)` †: a player leaves (its input, or its number, 2 to 4); player 1 has the whole keyboard back when no one shares it\n527:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the ca\n569:- `E.PLAYER_COLORS: #4a8aff, #ff4a4a, #4ad860, #ffd040` †: the players' colors: player 1 blue, 2 red, 3 green, 4 yellow (game.players)\n777:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game who\n---\n55:- 220 Views (projections); E.View: view\n59:- 368 Lighting; game.lights\n224:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n370:- `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity = 1, o)` †: radius in world units; intensity ~0.5..1.5. opts: { color: '#ffaa55' (both lightings), shadow: true (GPU lighting: walls and casters block it) }\n371:- `game.lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` †: something that blocks light (GPU shadows): a cylinder of radius r from the floor up to height top\n372:- `game.lights.heat(x, y, z, width, strength = 1)` †: heat shimmer above a point (GPU only). width in world units, strength ~0.5..1.5\n373:- `game.lights.on` †: true when the canvas lighting draws this frame: enabled, or standing in for GPU lighting the game turned on that can't draw (no WebGPU, still loading, a side view); gpu.fallback = false keeps such a frame unlit\n374:- `game.lights.refresh()` †: rebuild the darkness bands after changing dark, levels or glow (lights.dark = [r, g, b]; lights.refresh())\n375:- `game.lights.render(r)` †: darken the frame by the lights (the renderer calls it after the queue, when enabled)\n376:- `game.lights.ambient = .15` †: how lit unlit places are, 0 (black) .. 1\n377:- `game.lights.dark = [10, 6, 24]` †: the color of darkness, [r, g, b]\n378:- `game.lights.darkness = .9` †: how dark the darkest places get, 0..1 (the smooth style, E.style.trans 'alpha')\n379:- `game.lights.enabled = false` †: false (the default) turns the canvas lighting off\n380:- `game.lights.glow = [255, 200, 140, 0]` †: the color, [r, g, b, a], where light is brightest\n381:- `game.lights.glowAt = 1.7` †: the light level (1 = fully lit) above which it glows\n382:- `game.lights.levels = [.9, .7, .48, .26, .08, 0]` †: the darkness of each lighting band, darkest first (dithered between them)\n383:- `game.lights.list = []` †: this frame's lights from add()\n384:- `game.lights.screen = false` †: true measures lights on the screen, not the ground (side views and PlatformMaps do it by themselves)\n385:- `game.lights.tint = .32` †: how strongly lights add their own color, 0..1\n432:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a wa\n436:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written),\n481:- `game.cornerArea()` †: where the corner's buttons (menu and full screen, top right; the touch START) cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (r.W and r.H's space), or null while none show: keep a HUD clear of it\n483:- `game.enableGPU(o = {})` †: turn on WebGPU lighting: where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with its own ambient (game.lights.ambient) and the same lights. opts: { map, bands, ambient, fallback, ..\n504:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n540:- `game.lights` †: canvas lighting (lights.enabled, lights.add in draw)\n627:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n628:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n629:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n630:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n631:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01425XSAgNtFxkavLgWb6tw7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
