{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q9W5oVNXoRCVX8xQ6FMUnA","type":"tool_result","content":"sed: -e expression #1, char 1: unknown command: `,'\n *  (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's) */\nGame.prototype.allowJoin = function (o = {}) {\n  if (o === false) { this._join = null; this._lobby = null; _pClaim(this); return this; }\n  this._join = { max: clamp(o.max || 2, 2, 4), onJoin: o.onJoin || null, keys: o.keys !== false };\n  this._lobby = this._join.keys && this.screen.canvas ? new Input(_pStub(this), { join: ['Digit2'] }) : null;   // (listens for 2 while player 1 has the whole keyboard)\n  _pClaim(this); return this;\n};\n/** a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the\n *  left). Returns its input (null when four play already) */\nGame.prototype.addPlayer = function (o = {}) {\n  const P = this.players; if (P.length >= 4) return null;\n  const q = new Input(_pStub(this), Input.DEFAULT), n = P.length + 1;\n  Object.assign(q, { player: n, name: 'P' + n, color: E.PLAYER_COLORS[n - 1], pad: typeof o.pad === 'number' ? o.pad : null, half: o.keys ? 'right' : null, device: o.keys ? 'keyboard' : 'gamepad' });\n  for (const k of ['glyphs', 'deadzone', 'invertAimY', 'invertMoveX', 'invertMoveY', 'rumbleScale']) q[k] = this.input[k];   // (the player's settings: button symbols, dead zone, aim, the move stick, vibration)\n  q.lastDevice = q.device; if (q.pad !== null) { q.tick(0); q.consumeAll(); }   // (the buttons held as it joins, its Start among them, are no presses)\n  const I = P[0]; if (q.half && !I.half) { I._full = I.preset; I.half = 'left'; I.use(Input.halfKeys(I._full, 'left')); }   // player 1 moves to the left half\n  q.use(_pPreset(this, q));\n  if (!this.settings.spec('playerBindings')) this.settings.define({ key: 'playerBindings', group: 'Controls', type: 'bindings', value: () => ({}), apply: (g, v) => { for (const p of g.players.slice(1)) p.bindings = (v || {})[p.player] || {}; } });\n  q.bindings = (this.settings.playerBindings || {})[n] || {};\n  q._onBindings = b => this.settings.set('playerBindings', Object.assign({}, this.settings.playerBindings, { [n]: b }));\n  P.push(q); _pClaim(this);\n---\n3878:class Saves {\n\n## 10g. Weather\n\n- `E.WEATHER: rain, snow, ash, leaves, sand` †: the kinds of weather: n drops at amount 1, fall speed (world units a second), colors, streak (seconds of motion a drop's line shows), sway, rest (seconds it lies where it lands), splash, wind \n\n## 10k. Save slots\n\n- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), ver\n- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer versio\n- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing t\n- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n- `saves.game` †: its game\n- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n\n## 11. Humanoid rig\n\n- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n---\n1125:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, width, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1126:- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n1127:- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n1128:- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n1129:- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n1130:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), po\n1131:- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n1132:- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n1133:- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n1134:- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n1135:- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n1136:- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n1137:- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n1138:- `talk.game`: its game\n1139:- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n1140:- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n1141:- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n1142:- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n1143:- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n1144:- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n1145:- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n1146:- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n1147:- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n1148:- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n---\n493:- `game.menu(name, o)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('contro\n20:- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n73:- 832 Flow field; E.FlowField: flow\n834:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a \n835:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n836:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump\n864:   *  (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER,\n868:    if (typeof map === 'string') map = Input[map.toUpperCase()] || Input.DEFAULT;\n882:    /** preset: the layout last given to use() (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, SHMUP or your own) */\n1041:  _check(a) { if (!this.map[a]) warn('action:' + a, 'unknown input action \"' + a + '\". Known actions: ' + Object.keys(this.map).join(', ') + '. Add your own with new E.Game({ input: { ...E.Input.DEFAULT, ' + a + \": ['KeyQ'] } })\"); }\n1309:Input.DEFAULT = {\n2344:    if (typeof o.input === 'string') o.input = Input[o.input.toUpperCase()] || (warn('input:' + o.input, 'unknown input preset \"' + o.input + '\" (use DEFAULT, PLATFORMER or SHMUP)'), Input.DEFAULT);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"372a8089-f019-4acc-8f7a-e2e8dbdaefa1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:12:56.772Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"sed: -e expression #1, char 1: unknown command: `,'\n *  (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's) */\nGame.prototype.allowJoin = function (o = {}) {\n  if (o === false) { this._join = null; this._lobby = null; _pClaim(this); return this; }\n  this._join = { max: clamp(o.max || 2, 2, 4), onJoin: o.onJoin || null, keys: o.keys !== false };\n  this._lobby = this._join.keys && this.screen.canvas ? new Input(_pStub(this), { join: ['Digit2'] }) : null;   // (listens for 2 while player 1 has the whole keyboard)\n  _pClaim(this); return this;\n};\n/** a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 