{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TwnB6z4xrW3xqehhxWW1jn","type":"tool_result","content":"   *  step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style,\n   *  color }; E.Humanoid.hat adds one); weapon: 'sword' | 'gun' | 'staff' (E.Humanoid.weapon adds one); hood: true\n   *  (drawn in colors.hair); draw: { under(g, Q, rig), over(g, Q, rig) } the game's own drawing before and after the body\n   *  (Q: the joints on screen, [x, y, depth]: outfits, accessories); seed: its own random stream (blinks, its clock) */\n  constructor(o = {}) {\n    if (o.build && !BUILDS[o.build]) warn('build:' + o.build, 'Humanoid build \"' + o.build + '\" is unknown (chibi, heroic, bulky, skeleton)');\n    o = Object.assign({}, BUILDS[o.build] || {}, o);\n    /** o: its options, with the build's proportions and the defaults filled in (size, build, weapon, outfit, ...;\n     *  legUpper, torso, headR and the other lengths are at size 1) */\n    this.o = Object.assign({\n      legUpper: 6, legLower: 6, hipZ: 11.6, hipHalf: 1.9, footSpread: 1.9, torso: 8, shoulderHalf: 3.3, neck: 1.2, headR: 3.4,\n      armUpper: 4.6, armLower: 4.6, limbW: 2, torsoW: 3, lean: 0, hunch: 0, stride: 6.5, lift: 3.4, swing: 4, speedRef: 70,\n      weapon: 'sword', bladeLen: 11, cape: null, hood: false, eyeGlow: null, hat: null,\n      style: 'hd', size: 1, hair: 'short', outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'short', armor: false, cheat: .5\n    }, o);\n    /** trail: recent points of the blade (or fist) tip, for the swing's smear */\n    this._cheat = 0; this.trail = [];\n    if (typeof this.o.hair === 'string' || !this.o.hair) this.o.hair = { style: this.o.hair || 'short' };\n    /** hairPts: the long hair's simulated points (null until it has some) */\n    this._hairPts = null;\n    if (this.o.weapon && !HUMANOID_WEAPONS[this.o.weapon]) { warn('weapon:' + this.o.weapon, 'Humanoid weapon \"' + this.o.weapon + '\" is not on E.Humanoid.weapons (sword, gun, staff, a game\\'s own by \n4726:    if (draw) draw({ g, Sp, J, r, R: this.o.headR, c, dk: shade(c, -.3), H, rig: this, at: (f, rr, z) => Sp(J.head, f, rr, z) });   // (E.Humanoid.hats: at(forward, right, up) a point round the h\n4872:Humanoid.hats = HUMANOID_HATS;\n4881:Humanoid.hat = (id, draw) => { HUMANOID_HATS[id] = draw; return draw; };\nsed: -e expression #1, char 1: unknown command: `,'\n648:     *  headless game draws: o.draw); ctx: its 2D context (r.ctx is the same) */\n649:    this.buf = canvas || (o && o.draw) ? mkCanvas(8, 8) : null; this.ctx = this.buf ? ctx2d(this.buf) : null;\n696:    if (this.buf) { this.buf.width = this.W + 2; this.buf.height = this.H + 2; this.ctx = ctx2d(this.buf); this.ctx._c = null; }\n1551:      this._g.putImageData(this._img, 0, 0); r.ctx.drawImage(this._cv, 0, 0);\n1552:      if (lit) { this._g2.putImageData(this._img2, 0, 0); const c = r.ctx; c.save(); c.globalCompositeOperation = 'lighter'; c.drawImage(this._cv2, 0, 0); c.restore(); }\n1564:    r.ctx.drawImage(this._cv, 0, 0);\n411:- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, rim=true, flash=false,\n412:- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (\n413:- `r.actor({ hides })`: true: this actor counts as an x-ray occluder even when no x-ray actor asked for actors\n414:- `r.actor({ ghost })`: ghost.owner (any {x, y, z}, usually the actor itself) keeps its afterimages sorted behind the live body\n415:- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background character animating at a lower rate, as classic games' townsfolk do: a phone's frame\n416:- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\n421:- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\n423:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n429:- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n433:- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint, box, top} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray sil\n435:- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n441:- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\n446:- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n198:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n200:- `px.ddisc(g, cx, cy, r, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: soft disc that fades toward its edge (glows, smoke, dust): stepped alpha rings, or dithering in 'dither' style\n201:- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n202:- `px.dot(g, x, y, c)`: one pixel\n203:- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n205:- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n206:- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n207:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n208:- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n1179:- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0463c')\n1180:- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-bottom gradient, like Final Fantasy windows) or [top, bottom] colors. gradient: false for a flat fill.\n1181:- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n1182:- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)\n169:- `E.mix(h1, h2, t)`: the color t of the way from h1 to h2 ('#rrggbb')\n181:- `E.shade(h, a)`: shade('#336699', -0.3) darker, (+0.3) lighter. Hue-shifted like painted pixel art: darker drifts cool, lighter drifts warm\n191:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, defa","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"790df598-1fa9-4580-a2d1-2438b8b38416","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:17:48.