wer rate, as classic games' townsfolk do: a phone's frame\n416:- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\n421:- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\n423:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n429:- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n433:- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint, box, top} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray sil\n435:- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n441:- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\n446:- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n198:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n200:- `px.ddisc(g, cx, cy, r, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: soft disc that fades toward its edge (glows, smoke, dust): stepped alpha rings, or dithering in 'dither' style\n201:- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n202:- `px.dot(g, x, y, c)`: one pixel\n203:- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n205:- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n206:- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n207:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n208:- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n1179:- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0463c')\n1180:- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-bottom gradient, like Final Fantasy windows) or [top, bottom] colors. gradient: false for a flat fill.\n1181:- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n1182:- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)\n169:- `E.mix(h1, h2, t)`: the color t of the way from h1 to h2 ('#rrggbb')\n181:- `E.shade(h, a)`: shade('#336699', -0.3) darker, (+0.3) lighter. Hue-shifted like painted pixel art: darker drifts cool, lighter drifts warm\n191:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, defa","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TwnB6z4xrW3xqehhxWW1jn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
