{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjLhm5xFNmbVhgS8Cq83","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011mT7desm4tMhQFHUKBcXbJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='../exit-interview.json'; d=json.load(open(p))\nd['sourceInformation'].update({\n \"audio\": \"All written in code with no files: 14 original songs and 5 jingles in step notation with music at 10% by default, about 30 synthesized sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish voices made letter by letter through a band-pass filter\",\n \"testing\": \"As the brief allowed: headless scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, behind one command that prints only failures and a count; browser checks with a stand-in pad, touch profiles and audio probes; the AI Hub harness; screenshots only for what a script cannot judge; no subagents or workflows\"\n})\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"About 25. 12 came from the scripted tests: for example the attract timer that never fired, a mouse that could not lean, a results screen that swallowed the story's next press, a jog list that skipped its water cups, and tray gaps that left no way through. The rest came from screenshots: overlapping HUD, a towel across the face, poses that turned when bent over.\",\n \"3: attract mode never started, the mouse could not lean for player 1, and the story could stall on the results screen.\",\n \"The scripted playthrough of the whole game with real taps and bots, run once with a good bot and once with a passive player. A close second: every activity and tier against its star bands, which found most of the tuning and logic faults.\",\n \"The Firefox and WebKit smoke tests. They passed the first time and have not caught anything yet, though they cost little.\"\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n \"The exact fixed step and the headless draw: a whole five-day story plays in Node in minutes with the same results every time. After that, how much is already there: rigs with real motion capture, Mode 7, the road, rhythm, physics, and pause, settings and rebinding I did not have to write.\",\n \"Three wrong guesses. game.hook passes only dt, not (game, dt), which made an idle timer NaN. input.player is undefined until game.players has been read. And rig.spin is not trustworthy for a bent-over clip, so I read one heading from the hips for held poses.\",\n \"The Lean: one balance model with an intent layer that makes a stick, keys and a mouse each native, then the activity runtime on top that hosts a run in a session, Class, attract, the Games and a hub round.\",\n \"Reading a rig correctly in several views and facings at low resolution, and keeping a 10-foot HUD legible with a 5x7 font at 427 x 240. E.Rhythm also reads game.input directly, so per-player Class needed a proxy game object.\",\n \"The Dialog's hard-coded dark text shadow now follows talk.shadow in 3 places, and its box shadows follow it too, because the shadows smeared on a white box. Nothing else.\",\n \"A stable heading for bent-over poses in Mocap.drive, read from the hips, so a held Down Dog does not turn when its chest has no heading to trust.\"\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n \"The plan's tested recipes and verbatim lines. The tone was already there, and the numbers marked as tested were right: the balance table reproduced almost exactly on the first run.\",\n \"Space is both Effort and Jump on the Laundry Line, so I moved keyboard walking to W and mouse jumping to the right button. The file name also does not say how to write a SOURCE with a space, so I used WiiFit. The plan was tested on engine v0.88.0 and the handoff is v0.89.0, which caused no trouble.\",\n \"Tuning twelve activities without being able to feel them. Bots can hold a star band, but only judgment says whether a thumb will enjoy it.\",\n \"Resolve the Space conflict in the input table, say how to write a SOURCE with spaces in the file name, and add a short list of the feelings to check by hand for whoever can play it.\"\n]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\ndef sub(p, a, b):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    if a not in s: print('MISSING',p,a[:70]); return\n    open(p,'w').write(s.replace(a,b,1))\nsub('game/balance.js',\"const dx = (I.down('right') ? 1 : 0) - (I.down('left') ? 1 : 0), dy = (I.down('up') ? 1 : 0) - (I.down('down') ? 1 : 0);\",\"const dx = (I.down('right') ? 1 : 0) - (I.down('left') ? 1 : 0), dy = o.axisX ? 0 : (I.down('up') ? 1 : 0) - (I.down('down') ? 1 : 0);\")\nsub('game/activities/runtime.js',\"c.reader.read(dt, c.intent, { overPanel: !!(G.Dev && G.Dev.overPanel && G.Dev.overPanel()) });\",\"c.reader.read(dt, c.intent, { overPanel: !!(G.Dev && G.Dev.overPanel && G.Dev.overPanel()), axisX: ctx.def.leanAxis === 'x' });\")\nsub('game/data/activities.js',\"{ id: 'laundry', family: 'laundry',\",\"{ id: 'laundry', leanAxis: 'x', family: 'laundry',\")\nsub('game/data/activities.js',\"{ id: 'jog', family: 'jog',\",\"{ id: 'jog', leanAxis: 'x', family: 'jog',\")\nEOF\ngrep -n \"if (src === 'gamepad' && padOn)\\|intent.rawY = -pad\" game/balance.js | head -3 | cut -c1-160; node build.mjs | tail -1 | cut -c150-; python3 -c \"\nimport json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print(list(d.keys()),len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']))\"; timeout 100 python3 tests/tools/screens.py shots/s about 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Fill the exit interview, fix W-held lean, rebuild, reshoot About","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3555,"cache_read_input_tokens":715827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3555},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnosti