{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjNGpxtuWVuvRyxu2Txv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hand-in is complete, and the hook's objection is now answered. I re-read `STAGE.md`, `TASK.md` and PLAN section 18 from `work`, then checked the handed-in files directly: all 35 checks hold. The files were always in `work`, the folder that holds `STAGE.md`, which is the root `TASK.md` means. My shell had just moved into the dev folder.\n\n| Requirement | Result |\n|---|---|\n| File names, dev folder, `PROGRESS.md` | All in `work`, with the exact names `TASK.md` asks for |\n| Hub tags, session client first in `<head>` | Present and in order |\n| `exit-interview.json` | Parses, exact shape, no blank or placeholder answers |\n| Running page from `file://` | Opens on \"Wee Teeter\"; music at 10%; PlayStation glyphs by default |\n| Content | 12 activities with 2 tiers each, 14 songs, 5 jingles, 27 live Dev sliders, every planned scene |\n| Attract mode | Starts after 10 s idle; any input returns to the title |\n| Page behaviour | No errors, no network requests, no audio files, no TODOs or stubs in `game/` |\n\n**Last test runs:** rules 623 passed, browser 48, hub 9, none failed. No game code has changed since. The brief says to re-run only after code changes, so I didn't run them again. The one new file is the check script, `tests/tools/handin.py`.\n\n**Limits of that check:**\n- It confirms files, settings and behaviour. Section 18's judgment items, such as tone and originality, rest on the tests, screenshots and how the game was built.\n- Nobody has played it by hand, so the balance is tuned against bots only. A real controller, iPhone and TV were only tested through stand-ins.\n- To re-run the browser tests, run `npm install` in the dev folder first.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 22:10:37\n- **Source:** Wii Fit\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre:** Sports and fitness minigame collection inside a light life-sim routine\n- **Perspective:** Per activity: 2.5D fixed (brawler view) in the studios, three-quarter on the island, Mode 7 behind the skier, pseudo-3D road behind the runner, a steep view of the tray, side view on the laundry line\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge full engine v0.89.0 (Mode 7, road, physics and rhythm modules, Mocap with a cut clip set), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript in a single HTML file\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native look: 3D skeleton puppets drawn as crisp pixel art at ps1 resolution, moved into bright daylight. New art in code: Tare, Gerald, wooden mannequin joints, the Plate, rooms, tray, laundry, gates\n- **Animation:** The engine's Humanoid rigs driven by motion capture (Mesh2Motion, Quaternius, CMU), with a hand-posed body layer (side lunge, hula, step-up, rope walk) and a wobble layer on top\n- **Audio:** All written in code with no files: 14 original songs and 5 jingles in step notation with music at 10% by default, about 30 synthesized sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish voices made letter by letter through a band-pass filter\n- **Online:** AI Hub session in ghost mode (1 to 4 players, the Morning Class round) and local Class for 2 to 4 on one screen; no other network\n- **Testing:** As the brief allowed: headless scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, behind one command that prints only failures and a count; browser checks with a stand-in pad, touch profiles and audio probes; the AI Hub harness; screenshots only for what a script cannot judge; no subagents or workflows\n- **Research:** None beyond the plan, the engine's documents and the hub protocol README\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 25. 12 came from the scripted tests: for example the attract timer that never fired, a mouse that could not lean, a results screen that swallowed the story's next press, a jog list that skipped its water cups, and tray gaps that left no way through. The rest came from screenshots: overlapping HUD, a towel across the face, poses that turned when bent over.\n- **How many would be considered critical or game breaking?** 3: attract mode never started, the mouse could not lean for player 1, and the story could stall on the results screen.\n- **Most helpful test:** The scripted playthrough of the whole game with real taps and bots, run once with a good bot and once with a passive player. A close second: every activity and tier against its star bands, which found most of the tuning and logic faults.\n- **Least helpful test:** The Firefox and WebKit smoke tests. They passed the first time and have not caught anything yet, though they cost little.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The exact fixed step and the headless draw: a whole five-day story plays in Node in minutes with the same results every time. After that, how much is already there: rigs with real motion capture, Mode 7, the road, rhythm, physics, and pause, settings and rebinding I did not have to write.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Three wrong guesses. `game.hook` passes only dt, not (game, dt), which made an idle timer NaN. `input.player` is undefined until `game.players` has been read. And `rig.spin` is not trustworthy for a bent-over clip, so I read one heading from the hips for held poses.\n- **Most important thing built:** The Lean: one balance model with an intent layer that makes a stick, keys and a mouse each native, then the activity runtime on top that hosts a run in a session, Class, attract, the Games and a hub round.\n- **Hardest part:** Reading a rig correctly in several views and facings at low resolution, and keeping a 10-foot HUD legible with a 5x7 font at 427 x 240. `E.Rhythm` also reads `game.input` directly, so per-player Class needed a proxy game object.\n- **Changed in the engine:** The Dialog's hard-coded dark text shadow now follows `talk.shadow` in 3 places, and its box shadows follow it too, because the shadows smeared on a white box. Nothing else.\n- **One change:** A stable heading for bent-over poses in `Mocap.drive`, read from the hips, so a held Down Dog does not turn when its chest has no heading to trust.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The plan's tested recipes and verbatim lines. The tone was already there, and the numbers marked as tested were right: the balance table reproduced almost exactly on the first run.\n- **Confusing:** Space is both Effort and Jump on the Laundry Line, so I moved keyboard walking to W and mouse jumping to the right button. The file name also does not say how to write a SOURCE with a space, so I used WiiFit. The plan was tested on engine v0.88.0 and the handoff is v0.89.0, which caused no trouble.\n- **Hardest thing:** Tuning twelve activities without being able to feel them. Bots can hold a star band, but only judgment says whether a thumb will enjoy it.\n- **Would change:** Resolve the Space conflict in the input table, say how to write a SOURCE with spaces in the file name, and add a short list of the feelings to check by hand for whoever can play it.\n\nFiles are in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221037__x61bd7e/work`:\n- `WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037/` (dev files)\n- `PROGRESS.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4977,"cache_read_input_tokens":770690,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4977},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"27e02e7d-ea6f-40ee-9d53-6efefa754008","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:14:13.707Z","request_id":"req_011CgjNGpQuU2XQVu6qDPVyv"}
