{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjYAwy5JKPz8dcQpyE27","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EDEkqCzz79YcfjsgwokdfL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"me=$(pwd); for p in $(pgrep -f \"node tests/run.mjs all\"); do [ \"$(readlink /proc/$p/cwd)\" = \"$me\" ] && { echo \"stopping my run $p\"; kill \"$p\"; }; done; sleep 1; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='../exit-interview.json'; d=json.load(open(p,encoding='utf8'))\nd['testingFeedback'][0]=\"About 40. 20 came from the scripted tests: for example the attract timer that never fired, a mouse that could not lean, a results screen that swallowed the story's next press, a jog list that skipped its water cups, tray gaps that left no way through, a rope bot that stopped jumping a peg after one trip, Laundry Line on keys, which a modelled person could not finish, two Dev sliders that were not live, and two melodies that shared a phrase with the engine's songbook. The rest came from screenshots: overlapping HUD, a towel across the face, poses that turned when bent over.\"\nd['testingFeedback'][2]=\"The scripted playthrough of the whole game with real taps and bots, run once with a good bot and once with a passive player. A close second: a modelled person playing every activity through the real keyboard, mouse and stick paths, which found the keyboard rope. The late audit of every number in the plan also earned its keep.\"\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w',encoding='utf8'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"\nimport json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print('parses',len(d['testingFeedback']))\"; node build.mjs | tail -1 | cut -c150-; sha256sum ../WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037.html | cut -c1-16; rm -f tests/tools/_all.log; (node tests/run.mjs all > tests/tools/_all.log 2>&1; echo \"exit $?\" >> tests/tools/_all.log) &\ndisown; pgrep -f \"node tests/run.mjs all\" | wc -l","description":"Stop my own run, update