{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Monitor, Read, ToolSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\" A session-scoped Stop hook checks this condition.\n   - STAGE.md, word for word: \"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\"\n   - TASK.md asks for an original game inspired by Wii Fit, with:\n     - a title picked by RNG from 50 riffs (result: **Wee Teeter**);\n     - a single HTML file `WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037.html` in root (`work/`);\n     - dev files in the subfolder of the same stem;\n     - `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML, in an exact shape;\n     - Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in the chat reply AND the in-game About screen, with Usage as \"added on import\";\n     - all audio in code, music at 10% by default, gibberish voices;\n     - AI Hub session support plus local multiplayer, attract mode at 10 s idle, Dev Mode from pause with live sliders and reset;\n     - 10-foot controller-first UI with native keyboard and mouse;\n     - touch-only devices show \"Controller or keyboard required\".\n   - Process rules from TASK.md to keep following, verbatim:\n     - \"Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"\n     - \"Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\"\n     - \"The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\"\n     - \"Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\"\n     - \"Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check. Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"\n   - Other rules: commit or push only if asked (nothing is committed). Give short updates when asked \"say in a few words what you're doing\". Never send the user's email anywhere. Use they/them for people whose pronouns are unknown.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3D2dge engine v0.89.0 (`engine/my-3d2dge.js`): fixed 1/120 s step; headless Node via `vm`; E.Game, scenes, E.Shell, E.Dialog, E.Humanoid, Mocap.drive, E.Mode7, E.Road, E.Physics, E.Rhythm, E.TileMap, E.FlowField, game.saves.\n   - `game.hook(fn)` passes only `dt`. A custom input map replaces the preset.\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (client 1.4.0), ghost mode, own card, harness at 5 settings.\n   - The Lean model: `Balance`, `BotBrain`, `DeviceReader` filling one `intent`, per-device native input.\n   - Activity runtime: `makeRun`, `stepRun`, `endRun`, `drawRun`, hosted by session, attract, class, games and round scenes.\n   - Testing: Node `vm` load (`tests/lib.mjs`, option `after: {file: code}` for data-only tests) and Python Playwright (system Python) on `file://`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (dev folder `work/WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037/`; the shell cwd is currently this folder):\n   - `build.mjs`: `node build.mjs [out.html]`. **Do not pass flags as argv[2]** (`--quiet` became a file name). Writes `../<stem>.html`, `tests/hub/game.html` and `game/index.html`; injects `window.WEE_ABOUT` from `../exit-interview.json`.\n   - `game/files.json`: script order.\n   - `game/core.js`: G, INPUT (`cancel` includes Mouse2, added `walk`, `jump` has Mouse2), CLASS_INPUT, DEV_SPEC (27 sliders), game, Shell, G.Save, spineAge (`devAge` override), earnMinutes, tier2Open, deepLink, devMember, debug snapshot, `G.ABOUT = window.WEE_ABOUT || {}`.\n   - `game/balance.js`, `rigs.js` (Poser reads one heading from the hips via `heading(c,t)`), `art.js` (G.ROOMS), `ui.js` (Pills sets `G.activePills`; prompts wrap; Results), `audio.js` (14 SONGS, 5 JINGLES, sfx, Tone, babble, G.talk, G.say, G.mutter), `dev.js`, `main.js`.\n   - `game/data/`: lines, poses, charts, courses (laundry `par: 56, worst: 220`), trays, activities (laundry `leanAxis:'x', keyRate:2.5, keyHome:4, keyEase:{s:.74,A:.82}, dur:165`, gust 9; Windy Washday s 16.5, gust 9; tray dur 70/90), days, unlocks, island, README.\n   - `game/activities/`: runtime, hold, candle, rep (k 26, c 10), step, hoop, jog, slalom, tray, laundry.\n   - `game/scenes/`: session, title, attract, member (G.startDay, G.nextDay), arrival, island (`Isl.player`), bodycheck (`BC.live`), evening, tareday, games (G.gamesPhase), ending (+freeplay, G.endingPhase), about (G.aboutPages), class (G.classPodium, G.classIdle), round (G.Hub).\n   - `tests/run.mjs` groups: `rules|audit|plan|speech|browser|hub|all` (plus `plan --list`). `rules` and `all` include `planAudit` and `speechAudit`. `browser` runs `browser.py` and `devices.py`.\n   - Other tests: `tests/lib.mjs`, `tests/plan.mjs` (planAudit: 494 checks; speechAudit: new), `tests/browser.py`, `tests/devices.py` (a whole first day on pad only, keys only, mouse only), `tests/hub.py`, `tests/tools/{acts.mjs,gallery.py,handin.py,hubcheck.py,hubfull.py,one.mjs,poses.py,screens.py,shot.py}`.\n   - Engine changes: only Dialog text and box shadows follow `talk.shadow` (a diff against upstream showed 4 lines plus upstream's version strings).\n   - Latest edits, just made and **not yet built or fully tested**:\n     - `session.js`: Card Back now `leave(true)`; `exit()` sets `G.pendingLine = G.line('tare.quit')` if `phase==='play' && !d.restarting && d.from!=='dev' && !G.inSession`; `restart()` sets `d.restarting=true`.\n     - `title.js` and freeplay in `ending.js` speak `G.pendingLine`.\n     - `evening.js`: `else game.after(.8, ...mutter G.line('tare.gerald'), {auto:4.5,y:144})`.\n     - `island.js`: Tare's talk rotates by `q.chat%3` (favorite, tips, gertrude); added a Mount Posture sign using `G.DATA.lines.sign.mount`.\n     - `dev.js`: `n===1` gives pausedOne.\n     - `candle.js`: duelTare mutter during 'sing'.\n     - `art.js`: `sign.mirror` drawn in the Iron Room.\n     - `lines.js`: removed the unused `wardrobe`.\n   - `dev.js` pause counter, suspected broken:\n     ```js\n     let was = false;\n     game.hook('step', () => {\n       if (G.inSession) return;\n       const p = game.paused && !!game.scene && !!game.scene.pausable;\n       if (p && !was) { G.S.pauses = (G.S.pauses || 0) + 1; }\n       if (!p && was && !D.on && G.S && game.sceneName !== 'title') { const n = G.S.pauses; if (n === 3) G.pendingPauseLine = G.line('tare.paused', { n }); else if (n === 1) G.pendingPauseLine = G.DATA.lines.tare.pausedOne; }\n       was = p;\n       if (G.pendingPauseLine && !game.paused && !G.talk.open) { G.mutter('tare', G.pendingPauseLine, { face: 'judging' }); G.pendingPauseLine = null; }\n     });\n     ```\n   - `candle.js` relevant code:\n     ```js\n     if (!I.touched && t > 20 && !ctx.duel && !c.skill) { b.fx += 4; if (!c.toldOff && G.cue(ctx, c)) { c.toldOff = true; G.mutter('tare', G.DATA.lines.tare.candleCheat, {...}); } }\n     ...\n     if (c.flame <= 0) { if (ctx.cheat) c.flame = .4; else if (!c.relit) {...relight...} else { c.out = true; ... } }\n     ```\n   - `../exit-interview.json`, `../PROGRESS.md` (status plus a section 18 evidence ledger; its final-run line needs updating), `README.md`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Build failed on missing files: filtered with `existsSync` during development.\n   - `game.hook` passes only dt, so the idle timer became NaN and attract never fired: use `(a,b)=>typeof a==='number'?a:b`.\n   - `input.player` undefined stopped the mouse leaning: `(c.input.player || 1) === 1`.\n   - Results default focus \"Again\" swallowed presses and stalled the story: default focus is Done (`i:1`).\n   - Attract rewrote the save timestamp: title skips saving when `fromAttract`.\n   - `wait_for_function` hung in the harness: poll with evaluate.\n   - **My process mistakes:** `pkill -f \"__never__\"` (forbidden) and `pgrep -f \"node tests/run.mjs all\"` both matched my own shell (exit 144). Never use pkill. To find my processes, use `ps -eo pid,cmd | grep \"tests/ru[n]\"` plus a `/proc/$p/cwd` check.\n   - `node build.mjs --quiet path` wrote a file called `--quiet`: removed.\n   - Foreground `sleep` chains are blocked. This works: `timeout 585 bash -c 'until grep -q \"^exit\" tests/tools/_all.log 2>/dev/null; do sleep 10; done'`.\n   - Bent poses turned because of `rig.spin`: hips heading.\n   - Jog `break` on an unsorted list skipped cups: `continue`.\n   - Tray gap sensors left no way through: r 2.5, and a Dijkstra bot avoiding gaps.\n   - Rope bot locked into never jumping a peg after one trip: `if (c.fallT>0){c.tried={};return;}`.\n   - Keyboard rope unplayable for a modelled person: keyRate, keyHome, keyEase; `extraS = 10*max(0,eff-.6)`; worst 220.\n   - Dev sliders for rhythm windows and tray friction weren't live: made live.\n   - Tray and jog melodies shared a run of 8 intervals with the songbook: rewritten.\n   - About page overflow: `H = game.H-78`.\n   - Member Cards prompts covered the Back pill: chips reduced.\n   - Test harness issues: a stick must be set after the input tick; use `I.press('Pad7')` instead of `Act:walk`; set `G.Save.slot=null` for the damaged-save test.\n   - Hook feedback was repeatedly right: test on the final file, and evidence over self-assessment.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Last complete run before the current edits: `node tests/run.mjs all` gave 2224 passed, 0 failed, hash 1805a7b7790a5795; `handin.py` 36 ok. **That result is now stale because the code changed.**\n   - Current `node tests/run.mjs speech`: 96 passed, 11 failed:\n     ```\n     §7 heard in play: Tare, paused\n     §7 heard in play: Tare, pausedOne\n     §7 heard in play: Tare, candleCheat\n     §7 heard in play: Tare, suggest\n     §7 heard in play: birch, hello\n     §7 heard in play: alder, hello\n     §7 heard in play: question: Have you recently sat?\n     §7 said at its moment: the morning\n     §7 said at its moment: a third pause\n     §7 said at its moment: the plateau\n     §7 said at its moment: a controller left alone\n     ```\n   - Diagnoses, not yet verified:\n     - **Real bug, pause lines:** `game.hook('step')` likely doesn't run while paused, so pauses are never counted. Move the logic to `game.hook('input', ...)`, which runs paused too, then confirm the mutter still fires after resume.\n     - **Real bug, candleCheat:** an untouched player's flame goes out at about 17 s, before the 20 s check. Fix so the plan's moment happens, e.g. while `!I.touched && t<20 && !c.skill`, the flame doesn't go out (hold it at a small value); then re-check that passive stays under 1★ and \"one relight then it ends\" still holds.\n     - **Test driver gaps:**\n       - `suggest`: `run()` only taps while a modal talk is open, so Body Check's Continue pill is never pressed. Press confirm throughout Body Check runs.\n       - `hello`: drive the `arrival` scene for each instructor.\n       - Questions: vary `G.S.runs` across all (index is `(day+runs)%len`).\n       - \"the morning\" and \"the plateau\": random picks from a list, so check that the verbatim line is in its group and the group was heard, not that one specific line was spoken.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - `/goal` command: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n   - Stop hook 1: insufficient evidence; STAGE.md and TASK.md not shown being read; hand-in files in the parent `work` folder, not the current folder; PLAN completion was self-assessment.\n   - Stop hook 2: no check of PLAN section 18 against the final state beyond claims; judgment calls (tone, originality, no dense screens, controller-first); nobody played by hand.\n   - Stop hook 3: browser group not re-run after the last change; full suite predated the final Member Cards fix; open judgment items.\n   - Stop hook 4: not conclusive; tone and originality rest on judgment, feel never checked, \"a PLAN.md item (Tare's speech is tested only against a list of verbatim plan lines) was not shown to be complete\"; STAGE.md wording not checked against the finished state.\n   - Stop hook 5 (latest): \"The transcript does not establish that everything in PLAN.md doable on this computer is done... the hand-in checks confirm the HTML and interview file exist and parse, but do not verify the PLAN.md item about Tare's speech beyond a list of verbatim plan lines. Once the test run, hand-in check, and STAGE.md step are complete, the remaining gap is judgment-based content that the transcript shows cannot be verified here, so the stop condition is not clearly met.\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Fix the pause hook and the candle moment; fix the speechAudit driver and checks; get `node tests/run.mjs speech` to 0 failures.\n   - Update `../exit-interview.json` testing feedback BEFORE the final build:\n     - add the newly found issues: plan-verbatim lines that were never spoken (Gerald, \"Leaving early?\"), \"You are my favorite\" only reachable with Tips off, the pause counter never counting, the Candle line unreachable;\n     - adjust the count (about 45 total, about 25 scripted);\n     - optionally mention listening to what the game says as a useful test;\n     - decide whether the critical count stays at 4.\n   - `node build.mjs`; run `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder (`node_modules` was removed; check.mjs needs it).\n   - Run `node tests/run.mjs all` once on the final file, with no edits afterwards, in the background, logging to `tests/tools/_all.log` and appending `exit $?`. Before and after, compare `sha256sum` of the HTML. Then run `python3 tests/tools/handin.py` from the dev folder.\n   - Update the `../PROGRESS.md` final-run line and add the speech audit to the ledger.\n   - Clean up: `rm -rf shots node_modules tests/__pycache__ tests/tools/__pycache__ check-output tests/tools/_all.log`. Check that no process of mine remains.\n   - Final chat reply: map STAGE.md's sentences to the state, state the test results and the hand-in location, name the speech fixes, keep what needs a person clearly separate (feel on a real thumb is not doable on this computer; real controller, iPhone and TV are stand-ins per TASK.md, never required; quality of my own lines and songs is judgment), list deviations, and include all required sections matching `exit-interview.json`.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Answering Stop hook 5 about Tare's speech. I scanned for silent lines, wired them in (edits in section 3), and appended `speechAudit(check)` to `tests/plan.mjs`. It wraps `G.talk.say`, records all spoken strings, and drives body checks, Tare's Day, sessions, the island, evening, the Games, duels, endings, Class and attract for both instructors. It then checks each line group with `group(name,list)` and each named moment with `said(line)`. The last output was `96 passed, 11 failed`, listed in section 5. The cwd is the dev folder.\n\n   Text for the final reply, to keep in sync with `exit-interview.json` (update the Testing Feedback counts as above):\n   - **Source Information:**\n     - Date: 2026-11-04 22:10:37\n     - Source: Wii Fit\n     - Plan: PLAN.md\n     - Genre: Sports and fitness minigame collection inside a light life-sim routine\n     - Perspective: Per activity: 2.5D fixed (brawler view) in the studios, three-quarter on the island, Mode 7 behind the skier, pseudo-3D road behind the runner, a steep view of the tray, side view on the laundry line\n     - Tech: my-3D2dge full engine v0.89.0 (Mode 7, road, physics and rhythm modules, Mocap with a cut clip set), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript in a single HTML file\n     - Art Direction: The engine's native look: 3D skeleton puppets drawn as crisp pixel art at ps1 resolution, moved into bright daylight. New art in code: Tare, Gerald, wooden mannequin joints, the Plate, rooms, tray, laundry, gates\n     - Animation: The engine's Humanoid rigs driven by motion capture (Mesh2Motion, Quaternius, CMU), with a hand-posed body layer (side lunge, hula, step-up, rope walk) and a wobble layer on top\n     - Audio: All written in code with no files: 14 original songs and 5 jingles in step notation with music at 10% by default, about 30 synthesized sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish voices made letter by letter through a band-pass filter\n     - Online: AI Hub session in ghost mode (1 to 4 players, the Morning Class round) and local Class for 2 to 4 on one screen; no other network\n     - Testing: As the brief allowed: headless scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, behind one command that prints only failures and a count; a modelled person on each device path; one-device walkthroughs of a whole first day with a stand-in pad, real keys and a real pointer; touch profiles and audio probes; the AI Hub harness; screenshots only for what a script cannot judge; no subagents or workflows\n     - Research: None beyond the plan, the engine's documents and the hub protocol README\n     - Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n     - Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\n     - Usage: added on import\n   - **Testing Feedback:**\n     1. About 40. 20 came from the scripted tests: for example the attract timer that never fired, a mouse that could not lean, a results screen that swallowed the story's next press, a jog list that skipped its water cups, tray gaps that left no way through, a rope bot that stopped jumping a peg after one trip, Laundry Line on keys, which a modelled person could not finish, two Dev sliders that were not live, and two melodies that shared a phrase with the engine's songbook. The rest came from screenshots: overlapping HUD, a towel across the face, poses that turned when bent over.\n     2. 4: attract mode never started, the mouse could not lean for player 1, the story could stall on the results screen, and Laundry Line could not be finished on a keyboard.\n     3. The scripted playthrough of the whole game with real taps and bots, run once with a good bot and once with a passive player. A close second: a modelled person playing every activity through the real keyboard, mouse and stick paths, which found the keyboard rope. The late audit of every number in the plan also earned its keep.\n     4. The Firefox and WebKit smoke tests. They passed the first time and have not caught anything yet, though they cost little.\n   - **Engine Feedback:**\n     - Liked most: The exact fixed step and the headless draw: a whole five-day story plays in Node in minutes with the same results every time. After that, how much is already there: rigs with real motion capture, Mode 7, the road, rhythm, physics, and pause, settings and rebinding I did not have to write.\n     - Stuck or guessed wrong: Three wrong guesses. `game.hook` passes only dt, not (game, dt), which made an idle timer NaN. `input.player` is undefined until `game.players` has been read. And `rig.spin` is not trustworthy for a bent-over clip, so I read one heading from the hips for held poses.\n     - Most important thing built: The Lean: one balance model with an intent layer that makes a stick, keys and a mouse each native, then the activity runtime on top that hosts a run in a session, Class, attract, the Games and a hub round.\n     - Hardest part: Reading a rig correctly in several views and facings at low resolution, and keeping a 10-foot HUD legible with a 5x7 font at 427 x 240. `E.Rhythm` also reads `game.input` directly, so per-player Class needed a proxy game object.\n     - Changed in the engine: The Dialog's hard-coded dark text shadow now follows `talk.shadow` in 3 places, and its box shadows follow it too, because the shadows smeared on a white box. Nothing else.\n     - One change: A stable heading for bent-over poses in `Mocap.drive`, read from the hips, so a held Down Dog does not turn when its chest has no heading to trust.\n   - **Prompt Feedback:**\n     - Liked most: The plan's tested recipes and verbatim lines. The tone was already there, and the numbers marked as tested were right: the balance table reproduced almost exactly on the first run.\n     - Confusing: Space is both Effort and Jump on the Laundry Line, so I moved keyboard walking to W and mouse jumping to the right button. The plan says keys at 2.2/s score the same as a stick, but on the rope my modelled person fell constantly, so keys there move faster and the rope is a little kinder to them. The file name also does not say how to write a SOURCE with a space, so I used WiiFit. The plan was tested on engine v0.88.0 and the handoff is v0.89.0, which caused no trouble.\n     - Hardest thing: Tuning twelve activities without being able to feel them. Bots can hold a star band, but only judgment says whether a thumb will enjoy it.\n     - Would change: Resolve the Space conflict in the input table, recheck the keyboard claim on the rope, say how to write a SOURCE with spaces in the file name, and add a short list of the feelings to check by hand for whoever can play it.\n   - **Deviations to state:**\n     - Laundry Line: keyboard walking on W and mouse jumping on the right button; keys move faster on the rope and it's kinder to them; scoring par 56 s to worst 220 s; tier 2 a little gentler.\n     - Rail exercises: k 26, c 10.\n     - Tray Service: 70 s, and 90 s on tier 2.\n     - `node_modules` removed, so run `npm install` before re-running browser tests; nothing committed.\n   - **Files in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221037__x61bd7e/work`:** `WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037.html`, `exit-interview.json`, `WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037/`, `PROGRESS.md`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Fix the 11 `speech` failures, starting with the two suspected real bugs (move the pause counter from the `step` hook to the `input` hook; let the untouched-candle moment actually happen at 20 s), then correct the test driver gaps and re-run `node tests/run.mjs speech`. After that, follow the Pending Tasks order: update the interview, build, `npm install playwright@1.63.0`, run the full `node tests/run.mjs all` on the final file, run `handin.py`, update PROGRESS.md, clean up, and give the final reply.\n\n   Where I left off, from my last message: \"I'm wiring them all in, then adding a test that records everything the game actually says in a real run and fails if any group of lines stays silent.\" The latest output: \"96 passed, 11 failed\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build-v2--20261104-221037--x61bd7e-work/e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"8d2a720e-7ff8-4a5e-b6d0-4dfce9996fc7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:48:24.685Z","isSynthetic":true}
