{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M2KEq7mgT2tk5HPr2QNHYE","type":"tool_result","content":"['sourceInformation', 'testingFeedback', 'engineFeedback', 'promptFeedback', 'aiHub']\n[\n \"About 40. 20 came from the scripted tests: for example the attract timer that never fired, a mouse that could not lean, a results screen that swallowed the story's next press, a jog list that skipped its water cups, tray gaps that left no way through, a rope bot that stopped jumping a peg after one trip, Laundry Line on keys, which a modelled person could not finish, two Dev sliders that were not live, and two melodies that shared a phrase with the engine's songbook. The rest came from screenshots: overlapping HUD, a towel across the face, poses that turned when bent over.\",\n \"4: attract mode never started, the mouse could not lean for player 1, the story could stall on the results screen, and Laundry Line could not be finished on a keyboard.\",\n \"The scripted playthrough of the whole game with real taps and bots, run once with a good bot and once with a passive player. A close second: a modelled person playing every activity through the real keyboard, mouse and stick paths, which found the keyboard rope. The late audit of every number in the plan also earned its keep.\",\n \"The Firefox and WebKit smoke tests. They passed the first time and have not caught anything yet, though they cost little.\"\n]\n10:Final `node tests/run.mjs all`, on the handed-in build with no edits after it: 2224 passed, 0 failed (rules, browser, one-device days, hub, and tests/plan.mjs: 494 checks of PLAN.md sections 1 to 1\n15:| Title, file, dev folder | crypto RNG pick in the transcript; `tests/tools/handin.py` checks file name, place, title on screen |\n17:| Genre, perspective, engine | `tests/tools/handin.py`, engine 0.89.0; diff against upstream shows only 4 Dialog lines changed, plus upstream's own version strings |\n29:| About and chat | test: every field and answer on the About pages in full, none cut; handin.py: page data equals the exit interview |\n30:| Exit interview | handin.py: exact shape, parses, no pending answers |\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in \n110-{\n111-  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\":\n112-  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n113-  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n114-  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n115-  \"aiHub\": {\n116-    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n117-    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n118-    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n119-    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n120-    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n121-    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n122-    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n123-    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n124-    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n125-    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles,\n126-  }\n127-}\n128-The catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n129-\n130-Testing Feedback\n131-\n132-- How many issues did 