{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019GcbViYsGRfj2sJpAh15aa","type":"tool_result","content":"About 45. 25 came from the scripted tests: for example the attract timer that never fired, a mouse that could not lean, a results screen that swallowed the story's next press, a jog list that skipped its water cups, tray gaps that left no way through, a rope bot that stopped jumping a peg after one trip, Laundry Line on keys, which a modelled person could not finish, two Dev sliders that were not live, two melodies that shared a phrase with the engine's songbook, a pause counter that never counted, a Candle line nobody could reach, and plan lines that were written down but never spoken, such as Gerald's and \"Leaving early?\". The rest came from screenshots: overlapping HUD, a towel across the face, poses that turned when bent over.\n4: attract mode never started, the mouse could not lean for player 1, the story could stall on the results screen, and Laundry Line could not be finished on a keyboard.\nThe scripted playthrough of the whole game with real taps and bots, run once with a good bot and once with a passive player. A close second: a modelled person playing every activity through the real keyboard, mouse and stick paths, which found the keyboard rope. Two late audits also earned their keep: every number in the plan, and a test that records everything the game actually says in play and fails if a group of lines stays silent.\n/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221037__x61bd7e/work/WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037.html 1.80 MB\n95d2fee05572f920","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"a4eb1fcb-3eec-4052-a238-0d76333767b6","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:50:34.087Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"About 45. 25 came from the scripted tests: for example the attract timer that never fired, a mouse that could not lean, a results screen that swallowed the story's next press, a jog list that skipped its water cups, tray gaps that left no way through, a rope bot that stopped jumping a peg after one trip, Laundry Line on keys, which a modelled person could not finish, two Dev sliders that were not live, two melodies that shared a phrase with the engine's songbook, a pause counter that never counted, a Candle line nobody could reach, and plan lines that were written down but never spoken, such as Gerald's and \"Leaving early?\". The rest came from screenshots: overlapping HUD, a towel across the face, poses that turned when bent over.\n4: attract mode never started, the mouse could not lean for player 1, the story could stall on the results screen, and Laundry Line could not be finished on a keyboard.\nThe scripted playthrough of the whole game with real taps and bots, run once with a good bot and once with a passive player. A close second: a modelled person playing every activity through the real keyboard, mouse and stick paths, which found the keyboard rope. Two late audits also earned their keep: every number in the plan, and a test that records everything the game actually says in play and fails if a group of lines stays silent.\n/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221037__x61bd7e/work/WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037.html 1.80 MB\n95d2fee05572f920","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019GcbViYsGRfj2sJpAh15aa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
