{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JFkwPabbjUvdWe8RrGC5ub","type":"tool_result","content":"150:**Step Class** (`step`, `E.Rhythm`). A bench, an instructor, three Regulars behind you all stepping on the beat. Always four lanes in the order `arrows: true` draws: `lanes: ['stepL', 'stepD', 'stepU', 'stepR']`. Tier 1's charts use onl\n234:## 7. Cast and voice\n236:**Tone rules.** Short sentences. Sincere, polite, a little too personal. Translated-instruction-manual cadence. No sarcasm, no meanness, no profanity, no pop-culture jokes, no references to being a game. Praise that wobbles. Facts nobod\n238:**Tare** (talking scale; \"tare\" is the button that zeroes one). A white slab with two soft footprints on top, a small dial, short legs, cyan LED eyes on the front edge and 8 faces (neutral, happy, worried, smug, shocked, sad, asleep, ju\n263:**The instructors** are wooden artists' mannequins: smooth egg heads, ball joints, no blinking, infinite patience. The player picks one on Day 1; they differ in voice, palette and lines.\n265:- **Birch** (oak tones, tall, deep slow voice): \"Welcome. I am Birch. I'm made of wood, so I will be very patient and slightly warped.\" / \"Breathe in. ...I don't breathe. But I've read about it, and it sounds very good.\" / \"Keep your ba\n266:- **Alder** (pale maple, carved ponytail, warm bright voice): \"Hello! I'm Alder. I was a tree, and then I was a lot of very small decisions.\" / \"Wonderful! You're doing so well. Please stop shaking.\" / \"Everybody's body is different. Yo\n268:**The Regulars** (chibi rigs, each with their own palette and voice pitch; they fill backgrounds, toss hoops, set times):\n390:**Voices: Animalese-style gibberish, a sound per letter, on the voice bus.** `new E.Dialog(game, { voice: (ch, i, talk) => babble(talk.name, ch) })` (`talk.name` is the speaker the current `say` gave). `babble` makes a 60 to 90 ms oscil\n417:**Game settings** (`menu.settings`): `music` .1, `glyphs`, `voice` slider, Gentle Mode, Breath Hold/Toggle, Tare's Tips on/off. `menu.items`: Restart Session, Dev Mode. `menu.quit: 'title'`, autosaving first. `menu.controls` names the a\n608:- Sound: after a gesture, an `AnalyserNode` on the music bus is non-silent and `game.settings.music === .1` on fresh storage; the voice bus sounds during dialog; `OfflineAudioContext` renders `babble` non-silent; no audio files and no n\n624:| M1 | Lean, intent, devices, bots, Plate; `makeRig`; Tare and voice; studio scene; **Stork Stand** with Card and Results | Feels good on stick, keys and mouse. Bands hold. **Stop and tune here: it is the whole game** |\n644:- [ ] All audio from code; gibberish voices; music 10% by default (section 10)\n\n096 Nov  4 23:38 .\n096 Nov  4 22:10 ..\n097 Nov  4 22:10 PLAN.md\n819 Nov  5 03:13 PROGRESS.md\n219 Nov  4 22:10 STAGE.md\n526 Nov  4 22:10 TASK.md\n096 Nov  5 03:06 WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037\n423 Nov  5 02:50 WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037.html\n750 Nov  5 02:50 exit-interview.json\nREADME.md\nbuild.mjs\nengine\ngame\nnode_modules\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\nshots\ntests\nvendor\nBuild the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"5156c818-d128-4ffe-8d26-b778619cf4b9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:13:16.031Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"150:**Step Class** (`step`, `E.Rhythm`). A bench, an instructor, three Regulars behind you all stepping on the beat. Always four lanes in the order `arrows: true` draws: `lanes: ['stepL', 'stepD', 'stepU', 'stepR']`. Tier 1's charts use onl\n234:## 7. Cast and voice\n236:**Tone rules.** Short sentences. Sincere, polite, a little too personal. Translated-instruction-manual cadence. No sa