{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Zdkd3szhdWPUVnVCHucMf","type":"tool_result","content":"## 16. Testing\n\n**One command: `node tests/run.mjs [rules|browser|hub|all]`.** It prints only failures and one final line (`213 passed, 0 failed`). Rerun only the group whose code you changed. Use scripted checks first and screenshots only for what a script can't judge. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n**`rules` (Node, no browser, seconds).** Load engine, vendor and game files in a `vm` context with `window`, `addEventListener` and `location` stand-ins (✔ `Mocap` and clips load this way; see `engine/kits/test.mjs`). Drive with `game.advance` and `input.tap/hold`; read `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n- Lean model: each row of the section 3 table lands in its band (±10 points) with the bots, on 12 seeds.\n- Every activity, every tier: passive under 1★; average at least 1★; good at least 2★; finishes in its time; `game.errors` stays empty.\n- **Full scripted playthrough:** New Member through every scene to the Ending using real input taps and bots, all 12 activities played, Spine Age falls, Day 3 plateau holds, unlocks arrive, Free Play opens. Also a passive run (the worst player still reaches the end).\n- Saves: reload gives the same state; 3 members stay separate; a damaged save doesn't crash.\n- Same seed and same input give the same hash twice.\n- Attract: fires at 10 s idle (and not at 9.9), visits every playlist item, any input returns to title, no save or unlock changed.\n- Dev: every slider changes its live value; reset restores all; every jump target loads.\n- Class: 4 inputs, scores, podium. Hub logic with a fake `AIHub` object: same seed, same deal; time-up reports once; end stops input.\n- Data lint: every line, pose, clip name, activity and unlock referenced exists; no `TODO` or placeholder strings in `game/`.\n\n**`browser` (Playwright, one browser at a time, on the built file via `file://`, which needs no server):**\n- `node engine/tools/check.mjs <built file>` passes with no errors (and act on its look notes), at 1280×720.\n- **Controller stand-in ✔:** `add_init_script` replaces `navigator.getGamepads` with a `'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)'` pad in `mapping: 'standard'`. Check axes lean, `buttons[7].value` reads through `input.value`, ✕ confirms, prompts show ✕, Settings to Xbox shows A.\n- Keyboard and mouse: WASD nudges; pointer leans; hover moves focus in `Pills` and in the HTML menus; click activates; prompts change with the device.\n- Touch-only: a phone profile shows the notice and Settings button, no touch controls, and attract starts at 10 s behind it. iPhone profile on WebKit as a smoke test; also load in Firefox.\n- Sound: after a gesture, an `AnalyserNode` on the music bus is non-silent and `game.settings.music === .1` on fresh storage; the voice bus sounds during dialog; `OfflineAudioContext` renders `babble` non-silent; no audio files and no network requests at all (`page.on('request')`).\n- 1920×1080 screenshots for the 10-foot judgement of title, Plate, Card, results and island: look at them once per milestone.\n\n**`hub`:** copy the bundle to `tests/hub/game.html`, serve `tests/hub` with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is yours, then open `harness.html?game=game.html&` + each of: `players=1&auto=1`; `players=2&auto=1`; `players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, and print failing `checks`. Then open the game on its own and see it reach the title. Stop only your server, by its PID, never with `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\n\n**Sharing this computer:** keep one or two browsers open, keep every file in your own folder, don't read the folders beside it (other agents work there), never kill anything you did not start. \"Target closed\" or \"page crashed\" means memory ran out: run fewer browsers rather than retrying.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Build order\n\nEach milestone ends with a playable game and green tests. Keep the build and the tests working from M0 onward.\n\n| # | Build | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Fetch; `build.mjs`; `tests/run.mjs`; `INPUT`, Shell theme, settings; empty title and round scenes with the session wrapper | Harness passes on the empty game; music .1; `tests/run.mjs` prints its line |\n| M1 | Lean, intent, devices, bots, Plate; `makeRig`; Tare and voice; studio scene; **Stork Stand** with Card and Results | Feels good on stick, keys and mouse. Bands hold. **Stop and tune here: it is the whole game** |\n| M2 | Title, Pills, Member Card, Arrival, island, mats, Body Check, Day loop, evening, saves, Gerald, Spine Age; attract skeleton; Dev panel with Lean sliders | A day can be lived start to end |\n| M3 | Sun Flow, Quiet Candle, all three Rail exercises | Bots pass; poses read at 1080p |\n| M4 | Step Class, Hoop Hips, Coastal Jog | Bots pass; beat audible at default volume |\n| M5 | Slalom, Tray Service, Laundry Line | Bots pass |\n| M6 | Five-day script, Tare's Day, Gentle Games, duel, Ending, Credits, Free Play, wardrobe, full line bank, all music and sfx | Full playthrough test passes |\n| M7 | Class mode; the hub round with ghosts and card | Harness at all five settings; two-page play shows ghosts |\n| M8 | Full attract, full Dev Mode with Pose Viewer, About screen, tier 2s, Comfort, polish pass (particles, stamps, rumble, transitions: `game.go` with `fade: 'iris'`) | All groups green |\n| M9 | Final bundle, exit interview parses, About matches it, brief checklist below | Done |\n\n**If you truly run out of room, cut in this order and remove every trace (no stubs):** tier 2s except Eyes Closed → Tare's Day scene → Laundry Line → Coastal Jog → wardrobe items beyond three. Never cut: the Lean, Stork, Rail, Step, Candle, Slalom, Tray, the day loop, the ending, attract, dev mode, Class, the hub round, About.\n\n---","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"6c6dc8fd-3434-45d8-9c4e-ffb02597bd4c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:14:22.179Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## 16. Testing\n\n**One command: `node tests/run.mjs [rules|browser|hub|all]`.** It prints only failures and one final line (`213 passed, 0 failed`). Rerun only the group whose code you changed. Use scripted checks first and screenshots only for what a script can't judge. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n**`rules` (Node, no browser, seconds).** Load engine, vendor and game files in a `vm` context with `window`, `addEventListener` and `location` stand-ins (✔ `Mocap` and clips load this way; see `engine/kits/test.mjs`). Drive with `game.advance` and `input.tap/hold`; read `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n- Lean model: each row of the section 3 table lands in its band (±10 points) with the bots, on 12 seeds.\n- Every activity, every tier: passive under 1★; average at least 1★; good at least 2★; finishes in its time; `game.errors` stays empty.\n- **Full scripted playthrough:** New Member through every scene to the Ending using real input taps and bots, all 12 activities played, Spine Age falls, Day 3 plateau holds, unlocks arrive, Free Play opens. Also a passive run (the worst player still reaches the end).\n- Saves: reload gives the same state; 3 members stay separate; a damaged save doesn't crash.\n- Same seed and same input give the same hash twice.\n- Attract: fires at 10 s idle (and not at 9.9), visits every playlist item, any input returns to title, no save or unlock changed.\n- Dev: every slider changes its live value; reset restores all; every jump target loads.\n- Class: 4 inputs, scores, podium. Hub logic with a fake `AIHub` object: same seed, same deal; time-up reports once; end stops input.\n- Data lint: every line, pose, clip name, activity and unlock referenced exists; no `TODO` or placeholder strings in `game/`.\n\n**`browser` (Playwright, one browser at a time, on the built file via `file://`, which needs no server):**\n- `node engine/tools/check.mjs <built file>` passes with no errors (and act on its look notes), at 1280×720.\n- **Controller stand-in ✔:** `add_init_script` replaces `navigator.getGamepads` with a `'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)'` pad in `mapping: 'standard'`. Check axes lean, `buttons[7].value` reads through `input.value`, ✕ confirms, prompts show ✕, Settings to Xbox shows A.\n- Keyboard and mouse: WASD nudges; pointer leans; hover moves focus in `Pills` and in the HTML menus; click activates; prompts change with the device.\n- Touch-only: a phone profile shows the notice and Settings button, no touch controls, and attract starts at 10 s behind it. iPhone profile on WebKit as a smoke test; also load in Firefox.\n- Sound: after a gesture, an `AnalyserNode` on the music bus is non-silent and `game.settings.music === .1` on fresh storage; the voice bus sounds during dialog; `OfflineAudioContext` renders `babble` non-silent; no audio files and no network requests at all (`page.on('request')`).\n- 1920×1080 screenshots for the 10-foot judgement of title, Plate, Card, results and island: look at them once per milestone.\n\n**`hub`:** copy the bundle to `tests/hub/game.html`, serve `tests/hub` with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is yours, then open `harness.html?game=game.html&` + each of: `players=1&auto=1`; `players=2&auto=1`; `players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, and print failing `checks`. Then open the game on its own and see it reach the title. Stop only your server, by its PID, never with `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\n\n**Sharing this computer:** keep one or two browsers open, keep every file in your own folder, don't read the folders beside it (other agents work there), never kill anything you did not start. \"Target closed\" or \"page crashed\" means memory ran out: run fewer browsers rather than retrying.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Build order\n\nEach milestone ends with a playable game and green tests. Keep the build and the tests working from M0 onward.\n\n| # | Build | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Fetch; `build.mjs`; `tests/run.mjs`; `INPUT`, Shell theme, settings; empty title and round scenes with the session wrapper | Harness passes on the empty game; music .1; `tests/run.mjs` prints its line |\n| M1 | Lean, intent, devices, bots, Plate; `makeRig`; Tare and voice; studio scene; **Stork Stand** with Card and Results | Feels good on stick, keys and mouse. Bands hold. **Stop and tune here: it is the whole game** |\n| M2 | Title, Pills, Member Card, Arrival, island, mats, Body Check, Day loop, evening, saves, Gerald, Spine Age; attract skeleton; Dev panel with Lean sliders | A day can be lived start to end |\n| M3 | Sun Flow, Quiet Candle, all three Rail exercises | Bots pass; poses read at 1080p |\n| M4 | Step Class, Hoop Hips, Coastal Jog | Bots pass; beat audible at default volume |\n| M5 | Slalom, Tray Service, Laundry Line | Bots pass |\n| M6 | Five-day script, Tare's Day, Gentle Games, duel, Ending, Credits, Free Play, wardrobe, full line bank, all music and sfx | Full playthrough test passes |\n| M7 | Class mode; the hub round with ghosts and card | Harness at all five settings; two-page play shows ghosts |\n| M8 | Full attract, full Dev Mode with Pose Viewer, About screen, tier 2s, Comfort, polish pass (particles, stamps, rumble, transitions: `game.go` with `fade: 'iris'`) | All groups green |\n| M9 | Final bundle, exit interview parses, About matches it, brief checklist below | Done |\n\n**If you truly run out of room, cut in this order and remove every trace (no stubs):** tier 2s except Eyes Closed → Tare's Day scene → Laundry Line → Coastal Jog → wardrobe items beyond three. Never cut: the Lean, Stork, Rail, Step, Candle, Slalom, Tray, the day loop, the ending, attract, dev mode, Class, the hub round, About.\n\n---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014Zdkd3szhdWPUVnVCHucMf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgjc2Z2gW2cPtABEwucJj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0131hRnSQX3Cfnhz543gccsy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > tests/tools/_lines.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport { readFileSync } from 'fs';\nimport vm from 'vm';\nconst src = readFileSync('game/data/lines.js', 'utf8');\nconst ctx = { window: {}, console }; ctx.G = { DATA: {} }; ctx.window.G = ctx.G; ctx.My3D2dge = {};\nvm.createContext(ctx); try { vm.runInContext(src, ctx); } catch (e) { console.log('ERR', e.message); }\nconst L = ctx.G.DATA.lines; const out = []; const walk = (o, p) => { if (typeof o === 'string') out.push([p, o]); else if (Array.isArray(o)) o.forEach((x, i) => walk(x, p)); else if (o && typeof o === 'object') for (const k in o) walk(o[k], p ? p + '.' + k : k); };\nwalk(L, ''); console.log('total strings', out.length); let group = ''; for (const [p, s] of out) { if (p !== group) { console.log('## ' + p); group = p; } console.log(s); }\nEOF\nnode tests/tools/_lines.mjs | cut -c1-170","description":"Dump every line of the game's writing for reading"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4102,"cache_read_input_tokens":55952,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4102},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"26db3ed3-7444-45b7-a1f0-f3c37f5f23e1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:14:25.466Z","request_id":"req_011Cgjc2Yd8YqUyEdpUBE7RY","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0131hRnSQX3Cfnhz543gccsy":{"command":"cat > tests/tools/_lines.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport { readFileSync } from 'fs';\nimport vm from 'vm';\nconst src = readFileSync('game/data/lines.js', 'utf8');\nconst ctx = { window: {}, console }; ctx.G = { DATA: {} }; ctx.window.G = ctx.G; ctx.My3D2dge = {};\nvm.createContext(ctx); try { vm.runInContext(src, ctx); } catch (e) { console.log('ERR', e.message); }\nconst L = ctx.G.DATA.lines; const out = []; const walk = (o, p) => { if (typeof o === 'string') out.push([p, o]); else if (Array.isArray(o)) o.forEach((x, i) => walk(x, p)); else if (o && typeof o === 'object') for (const k in o) walk(o[k], p ? p + '.' + k : k); };\nwalk(L, ''); console.log('total strings', out.length); let group = ''; for (const [p, s] of out) { if (p !== group) { console.log('## ' + p); group = p; } console.log(s); }\nEOF\nnode tests/tools/_lines.mjs | cut -c1-170","description":"Dump every line of the game's writing for reading"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0131hRnSQX3Cfnhz543gccsy","type":"tool_result","content":"total strings 325\n## boot\nZeroing the scale\nSanding the instructors\nCounting the ducks\nTelling the hippo\n## arrival\nYou have been gifted a five-day stay at the Institute for Gentle Improvement. The card isn't signed. It only says: 'You know why.'\n## motto\nGently, Or Not At All.\n## tare.hello\nOh! Feet. Good morning, feet.\nYou came back. I wasn't worried. I was just standing here, on the floor, where I live.\nIt has been one day since you last stepped on me. I counted it twice to be sure.\nGood morning. I have been awake. I am always awake. It is fine.\nThere you are. I knew it was you. Nobody else stands like that.\nWelcome back. I saved your number. It was not hard. There is only one.\nHello. I heard you coming from the bungalow. That is not a comment.\nOh, good. I was about to start talking to the floor again.\n## tare.first\nHello. I am Tare. I am a scale. Please step on me.\nI will be measuring you. Please do not take it personally. I take it personally.\n## tare.still\nPlease stand still. Stiller. That was the wrong way.\nStand still, please. Like a lamp.\nDo not move. I will tell you when. I will not tell you when.\nA little less of that, please.\n## tare.leanTest\nNow lean. I will watch. I am very low down.\nLean where I say. Do not lean where I do not say.\n## tare.leanPraise\nYou lean beautifully. Like a tower people visit.\nYou put more weight on your left foot. Your right foot has noticed.\nYour balance is very interesting. I wrote that down. I cannot write.\nYou swayed. It was a nice sway. Please do not do it again.\nThat was almost the same as yesterday. I remember yesterday.\nYour right side is doing most of it. Your left side should thank it.\n## tare.number\nI am not allowed to say whether this is good. It is a number.\nThat is your number. I checked it. I am very sure of it. Please do not look at me like that.\nNumbers are only numbers. This one is yours.\nI have told you the number. I will not tell anybody else. I do not know anybody else.\n## tare.spineDown\nThat's younger than yesterday! Your spine has been through a lot.\nYounger again. I do not know how this works. I am only a scale.\nYour spine is going backwards. This is what we want.\nYour spine has lost a year. Do not go looking for it.\n## tare.spineSame\nIt hasn't moved. Numbers rest too.\nLet's call it 71. It doesn't go higher. It's not allowed.\nThe same as yesterday. I find that restful. Do you find that restful?\nNo change. I want you to know I noticed anyway.\n## tare.gertrude\nGertrude's Spine Age is 19. I mention this only for the data.\nGertrude is 19, in the spine. I have asked her how. She said, \"Thursday.\"\nFor comparison, Gertrude: 19. I am not comparing. I said \"for comparison\" by accident.\n## tare.favorite\nYou are my favorite. You are also my only.\nI had a dream last night. You were standing on me. It was just that.\nI would like to say something. I have forgotten it. It was about you.\nDo you think about me during the day? You do not have to answer. The answer is a number.\n## tare.idle\nAre you still there? I can feel you not standing on me.\nIt is quiet. I am choosing to find that relaxing.\nI can wait. Waiting is most of what I do.\nIf you are thinking about stretching, that also counts. It does not count.\n## tare.absent\nIt has been {n} days. I kept your spot warm. I am not able to generate heat.\n## tare.paused\nYou paused. That's {n} times today. I'm not counting. Three.\n## tare.pausedOne\nYou paused. That is fine. Everyone needs to look at something else sometimes.\n## tare.star0\nYou finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\nThat was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\nYou were there for all of it. That is what I will tell people.\nIt is not a race. If it were a race, this is the part I would not mention.\n## tare.star1\nGood effort! I could tell it was effort.\nOne star. I polished it myself. I do not have hands.\nThat was something. I have decided it was good.\nYou did that on purpose. I could tell. Well done.\n## tare.star2\nWell done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.\nTwo stars. That is one more than one.\nVery nice. Please do it again sometime when I am looking. I am always looking.\nYou have improved. I noticed before anybody. There is nobody else.\n## tare.star3\nYou barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don't do that.\nThree stars. There is no fourth. I checked. I wanted to give you one.\nPerfect. I do not know what to do with my feelings. I put them on the dial.\nThat was very good. I am going to stand here and think about it.\n## tare.fall\nYou fell. That's okay. The floor was expecting you.\nThat was a fall. It was a good one. You should hear it from me first.\nThe floor says hello.\nUp you get. Nobody saw. I saw.\n## tare.quit\nLeaving early? That's fine. I will just file this under 'Thursday.'\nYou can stop whenever you want. I will be right here, knowing about it.\nAll right. It was almost a session.\n## tare.night\nSleep well. I'll be out here. In the dark. Being accurate.\nGood night. I will keep the number safe. Nobody will come for it.\nSleep on your back, or your side, or however you like. I will not be checking. I cannot reach.\nRest. Your spine works nights.\n## tare.earlyBed\nBed already? It is still today. All right. I will tell today.\nYou still have sessions left. I will hold them for you. They will not keep.\nGoing to bed early is also a kind of exercise. It is not.\n## tare.gerald\nGerald has swallowed your minutes. He looks pleased. He always looks like that. He's ceramic.\nGerald took them. He does not give them back. That is the whole arrangement.\nClink. That is the sound of you improving, according to Gerald.\nGerald does not speak, but I believe he is proud. I believe it very hard.\n## tare.tips\nTip: Drink water. Your body is mostly water. The rest is opinions.\nTip: If you can't touch your toes, bring your toes closer.\nTip: Stretch before bed. Or after bed. Or in bed. I am not in your bed.\nTip: Sitting is just standing with fewer steps.\nTip: Breathing is best done regularly. Most people have found this.\nTip: A short walk is a long walk that has given up early. That is also fine.\nTip: Stand up straight. Now stop thinking about it. Now you are thinking about it.\nTip: The stairs are there whether you use them or not.\nTip: Your knees are listening. Speak well of them.\nTip: Eat a vegetable. Any vegetable. They do not check.\nTip: Rest days are important. Today is not one. I looked.\nTip: If you feel a stretch, that is your body telling you something. Do not ask what.\n## tare.gentle\nGentle Mode is on. I won't tell anyone. I don't know anyone.\n## tare.plateau\nWe call this the plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.\nYour number has not moved today. That is the plateau. People have camped here.\nThe plateau is very flat. That is how you know it is one.\n## tare.catchup\nOh. Look at that. It all came at once. I knew it would. I did not know it would.\nYour spine has caught up with you. It was only walking behind.\n## tare.candleCheat\nDid you put the controller down? I can tell. This is not that kind of stillness.\n## tare.nod\nGertrude nodded at you. I saw it. That was the reward. There is no other reward.\n## tare.suggest\nToday I suggest {a}. I don't know why. I just have a feeling. I have one feeling.\nMy suggestion today is {a}. It pays half as much again. Gerald insisted.\nToday, please consider {a}. I have marked the mat with a star. I had help.\n## tare.bowTie\nI am wearing a bow tie. It is because of your minutes. Please say nothing. Please notice.\n## tare.attract\nNobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\nThe room is very interested. It has not said so.\nThis is called a demonstration. I am demonstrating to the floor.\nEverybody is at lunch. I will keep going.\nIf somebody comes in, please act normal.\n## tare.attractBack\nOh! You're back. I wasn't doing anything.\n## tare.day5\nToday is the Gentle Games. You have prepared for this. You have been here four days.\nThere will be bunting. I am told it is very gentle bunting.\n## tare.gameOn\nThe Gentle Games! Everybody is very calm about it.\nFirst event. Please compete gently.\n## tare.class\nA class! Several feet. I do not know where to look. I look up. Always up.\nEverybody please stand on your own mat. I will be reading you all at once.\n## tare.podium\nI have read the results. They are all numbers. Some are larger.\nEverybody did something. Here is who did it most.\n## tare.afterDays\nYou are still here. The stay was five days. I did not want to bring it up.\nAnother day. I was not expecting you. I was expecting you.\nWelcome back. Nothing has changed. I have been very careful about that.\n## tareDay\nToday I must be recalibrated. It is a routine procedure. I have been dreading it for a year.\nPlease come to Reception. The big scale is there. It is my mother. It is a very old scale.\nPlease stand me on her. Then press the button to read it.\nI will close my eyes. I am not able to close my eyes.\n## tareRead\nThree grams.\nIt's the feelings. They're dense.\nPlease do not tell Gerald. He would swallow it.\nThank you for reading me. Nobody has ever read me. I read everybody.\n## questions.q\nHave you recently sat?\n## questions.a\nYes\nDefine recently\n## questions.r\nI can tell. It was a good sit.\nIt is a word that means recently.\n## questions.q\nDo stairs ever surprise you?\n## questions.a\nOften\nOnly the last one\n## questions.r\nThey are very sudden.\nIt is always the last one. It is why it is last.\n## questions.q\nDo you make a small noise when you stand up?\n## questions.a\nYes\nNo (this is a lie)\n## questions.r\nThank you for your honesty. I also hear it.\nI have marked this down as yes.\n## questions.q\nOn a scale of one to me, how do you feel?\n## questions.a\nOne\nMe\n## questions.r\nI see. I will try not to be hurt.\nThat is the nicest thing anyone has said on me.\n## questions.q\nWhen did you last look at your feet?\n## questions.a\nJust now\nI'd rather not\n## questions.r\nThey look fine from here. I am very close to them.\nI understand. I will keep an eye on them for you.\n## questions.q\nDo you know where your hips are?\n## questions.a\nRoughly\nWho is asking\n## questions.r\nRoughly is what most people say.\nA scale. A scale is asking.\n## questions.q\nHave you thought about your posture just now?\n## questions.a\nNow I have\nPlease stop\n## questions.r\nEverybody sits up at this point. You sat up.\nI will stop. I have stopped. You are still sitting up.\n## reading\nToday you weigh {d} ducks. That is a normal number of ducks.\nYou weigh {d} ducks. I weighed them twice. The ducks did not mind.\nToday: {d} ducks. Do not picture them. Now you are picturing them.\nThe reading is {d} ducks. A goose would be different. Please do not ask about the goose.\n## ending.reveal\nI should tell you something.\nThe card. The one that wasn't signed. That was me.\nI don't have hands. It took three years.\nI sent one to everybody. You're the one who came.\n## ending.leave\nNow step off. Go on. I'll be here.\nI'm a scale. That's the whole job.\n## ending.low\nGertrude says you may have the hat. She has another one. She has been waiting since Thursday.\n## ending.mid\nYour spine has stopped asking questions.\n## ending.high\nCome back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.\n## ending.free\nThe Institute is open. It was always open. I would have told you, but you did not ask.\n## gertrudeWin\nWell done, dear. I've been waiting since Thursday.\n## gertrudeLose\nThat's all right, dear. I had a head start. I started in 1961.\n## duel\nGull!\nThat is a blender. Do not look at the blender.\nA conga line. They are being very gentle about it.\nFireworks. Somebody has been saving them.\nI will now sing. I have been practising. It is one note.\nGoose. I told you about the goose.\n## duelTare\nLa. La. La. La. La. La. La.\n## sign.laundry\nPlease do not walk on the laundry line. Walking on the laundry line: 10:30 daily.\n## sign.iron\nYou Have Been Doing That Wrong\n## sign.mirror\nObjects In Mirror Are You\n## sign.juice\nJuice. Ask About The Olive.\n## sign.reception\nPlease Wait To Be Measured\n## sign.pier\nAerobics Pier. Mind The Gulls.\n## sign.deck\nQuiet Please. Quieter.\n## sign.mount\nMount Posture. Elevation: Good.\n## thoughts\nDid you lock the door?\nWhat is a lumbar?\nIs that my knee?\nDennis.\nYou left the stove on in 2014.\nWho sent that card?\nAm I breathing right now?\nNow I'm breathing on purpose.\nOlive?\nDo hippos sleep?\nWhat is the goose doing?\nIs it still Thursday?\n## birch.voice\nbirch\n## birch.name\nBirch\n## birch.hello\nWelcome. I am Birch. I'm made of wood, so I will be very patient and slightly warped.\n## birch.breathe\nBreathe in. ...I don't breathe. But I've read about it, and it sounds very good.\n## birch.demo\nKeep your back straight. Mine was sanded.\nNice. Now hold that until it stops being nice.\nYou're shaking. This means it's working. Or you're cold.\nWatch me once. I will do it slowly. I do everything slowly.\nI have held this pose since the shop.\nIt is simple. I will not say easy. I am a professional.\n## birch.more\nTwo more. I said that two reps ago. It is still true.\n## birch.moreFirst\nYou're doing so well, so I've added some.\n## birch.other\nOther way. The hoop does not mind. Your hips may have a view.\n## birch.lean\nLean toward the ring. Slowly. I have been told I am slow. It was a compliment.\n## birch.hold\nHold. Good. Now keep doing that, forever, or until I say.\n## birch.recover\nA gull has landed on you. Do not be flattered. Lean away from it.\n## birch.good\nGood. That was good. I do not say this often. I do not say many things.\n## birch.tired\nYou look tired. I do not get tired. I get damp.\n## alder.voice\nalder\n## alder.name\nAlder\n## alder.hello\nHello! I'm Alder. I was a tree, and then I was a lot of very small decisions.\n## alder.breathe\nAnd breathe in! Lovely. You look like someone breathing.\n## alder.demo\nWonderful! You're doing so well. Please stop shaking.\nEverybody's body is different. Yours is the one wobbling.\nLet's hold this for a moment. A moment is eleven seconds.\nSmile. It relaxes the jaw. ...Not like that.\nThis next pose is the Stork. I knew a stork. We didn't speak.\nFollow me! I am very easy to follow. I have no knees to speak of.\n## alder.more\nTwo more! You did not hear me say that earlier, but I thought it.\n## alder.moreFirst\nYou're doing so well, so I've added some.\n## alder.other\nOther way! Your hips will thank you. They will not. They do not speak.\n## alder.lean\nLean over to the ring! Lovely. A little more. That is too much. Lovely.\n## alder.hold\nHold it there! You are doing it. You are still doing it. You are very still doing it.\n## alder.recover\nOh! A gull. How nice for you. Lean the other way, please!\n## alder.good\nThat was wonderful! I have been told to say that. It was also true.\n## alder.tired\nYou look tired! That's the muscles saying thank you. Please stop them.\n## regulars.gertrude.name\nGertrude\n## regulars.gertrude.voice\ngertrude\n## regulars.gertrude.lines\nYou're doing fine, dear. I've been standing here since Thursday.\nI'm eighty-seven. My spine is nineteen. We don't really talk.\nStand up straight, dear. Not for me. I just like to see it.\nI had a hat like yours. I have it still. I have all the hats.\nI do not do the exercises any more. I only do the standing.\n## regulars.dennis.name\nDennis\n## regulars.dennis.voice\ndennis\n## regulars.dennis.lines\nI'm only here for the blender. Don't tell the scale.\nOlive?\nPeople ask why the olives. I ask why the people.\nI used to exercise. It was a Tuesday.\nThis juice has never been near a fruit. It is very calming.\n## regulars.marisol.name\nMarisol\n## regulars.marisol.voice\nmarisol\n## regulars.marisol.lines\nMorning! I've already done today. I'm on to tomorrow.\nKeep your cadence up! I don't know what yours is. Keep it up.\nI ran around the island twice while you read this.\nTomorrow's weather is lovely. I was just there.\n## regulars.kevin.name\nYoung Kevin\n## regulars.kevin.voice\nkevin\n## regulars.kevin.lines\nEverybody calls me Young Kevin. There was an older Kevin. We don't talk about how he got so flexible.\nI'm fifty-two. It's a very young fifty-two.\nI'm thinking of taking up the rope. I have been thinking of it for nine years.\n## regulars.okafor.name\nMr. Okafor\n## regulars.okafor.voice\nokafor\n## regulars.okafor.lines\nA hoop is just a circle that believes in you.\nHips first! Everything else will catch up. Or it will not. Hips first!\nThis shirt is called Tuesday in the Tropics. I have a Wednesday as well.\n## regulars.lou.name\nLou\n## regulars.lou.voice\nlou\n## regulars.lou.lines\nI'm on a five-minute break. It's been a good one. Three years in March.\nWake me if anything changes. Nothing will. That is why I chose this bench.\nThey tell me this bench is very good for the back. I have not checked.\n## regulars.twins.name\nThe Twins\n## regulars.twins.voice\ntwins\n## regulars.twins.lines\nWe're not related.\nWe've checked.\nWe do everything at the same time. We have not discussed it.\nPeople say we look alike. We do not see it. We do not look at each other.\n## slalomTimes\nGertrude\nShe walked.\nMarisol\nUphill, she says.\nYoung Kevin\nHe stopped to rest.\nLou\nHe is still on the chairlift.\n## nicknames\nGentle Doug\nSir Slouch\nMs. Almost\nThe Other Pat\nBig Linda\nMostly Paul\nTall Enough Ann\nSoft Gary\nDame Tilt\nUncle Maybe\nQuiet Sue\nYoung Barry\nNearly Nora\nWobbly Ted\nMadame Pause\nLord Lumbar\n## class.titles\nMost Still\nBest Wobble\nParticipated\nAlso There\n## class.join\nPress Start on a pad, or 2 on the keyboard, to take a mat.\n## hubTitles.Stillness\nMost Still\n## hubTitles.Strength\nBest Form\n## hubTitles.Cardio\nMost Cardio\n## hubTitles.Balance\nBest Wobble","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"1627c0f0-71b9-4eb9-a480-da602c01b52e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:14:25.504Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total strings 325\n## boot\nZeroing the scale\nSanding the instructors\nCounting the ducks\nTelling the hippo\n## arrival\nYou have been gifted a five-day stay at the Institute for Gentle Improvement. The card isn't signed. It only says: 'You know why.'\n## motto\nGently, Or Not At All.\n## tare.hello\nOh! Feet. Good morning, feet.\nYou came back. I wasn't worried. I was just standing here, on the floor, where I live.\nIt has been one day since you last stepped on me. I counted it twice to be sure.\nGood morning. I have been awake. I am always awake. It is fine.\nThere you are. I knew it was you. Nobody else stands like that.\nWelcome back. I saved your number. It was not hard. There is only one.\nHello. I heard you coming from the bungalow. That is not a comment.\nOh, good. I was about to start talking to the floor again.\n## tare.first\nHello. I am Tare. I am a scale. Please step on me.\nI will be measuring you. Please do not take it personally. I take it personally.\n## tare.still\nPlease stand still. Stiller. That was the wrong way.\nStand still, please. Like a lamp.\nDo not move. I will tell you when. I will not tell you when.\nA little less of that, please.\n## tare.leanTest\nNow lean. I will watch. I am very low down.\nLean where I say. Do not lean where I do not say.\n## tare.leanPraise\nYou lean beautifully. Like a tower people visit.\nYou put more weight on your left foot. Your right foot has noticed.\nYour balance is very interesting. I wrote that down. I cannot write.\nYou swayed. It was a nice sway. Please do not do it again.\nThat was almost the same as yesterday. I remember yesterday.\nYour right side is doing most of it. Your left side should thank it.\n## tare.number\nI am not allowed to say whether this is good. It is a number.\nThat is your number. I checked it. I am very sure of it. Please do not look at me like that.\nNumbers are only numbers. This one is yours.\nI have told you the number. I will not tell anybody else. I do not know anybody else.\n## tare.spineDown\nThat's younger than yesterday! Your spine has been through a lot.\nYounger again. I do not know how this works. I am only a scale.\nYour spine is going backwards. This is what we want.\nYour spine has lost a year. Do not go looking for it.\n## tare.spineSame\nIt hasn't moved. Numbers rest too.\nLet's call it 71. It doesn't go higher. It's not allowed.\nThe same as yesterday. I find that restful. Do you find that restful?\nNo change. I want you to know I noticed anyway.\n## tare.gertrude\nGertrude's Spine Age is 19. I mention this only for the data.\nGertrude is 19, in the spine. I have asked her how. She said, \"Thursday.\"\nFor comparison, Gertrude: 19. I am not comparing. I said \"for comparison\" by accident.\n## tare.favorite\nYou are my favorite. You are also my only.\nI had a dream last night. You were standing on me. It was just that.\nI would like to say something. I have forgotten it. It was about you.\nDo you think about me during the day? You do not have to answer. The answer is a number.\n## tare.idle\nAre you still there? I can feel you not standing on me.\nIt is quiet. I am choosing to find that relaxing.\nI can wait. Waiting is most of what I do.\nIf you are thinking about stretching, that also counts. It does not count.\n## tare.absent\nIt has been {n} days. I kept your spot warm. I am not able to generate heat.\n## tare.paused\nYou paused. That's {n} times today. I'm not counting. Three.\n## tare.pausedOne\nYou paused. That is fine. Everyone needs to look at something else sometimes.\n## tare.star0\nYou finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\nThat was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\nYou were there for all of it. That is what I will tell people.\nIt is not a race. If it were a race, this is the part I would not mention.\n## tare.star1\nGood effort! I could tell it was effort.\nOne star. I polished it myself. I do not have hands.\nThat was something. I have decided it was good.\nYou did that on purpose. I could tell. Well done.\n## tare.star2\nWell done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.\nTwo stars. That is one more than one.\nVery nice. Please do it again sometime when I am looking. I am always looking.\nYou have improved. I noticed before anybody. There is nobody else.\n## tare.star3\nYou barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don't do that.\nThree stars. There is no fourth. I checked. I wanted to give you one.\nPerfect. I do not know what to do with my feelings. I put them on the dial.\nThat was very good. I am going to stand here and think about it.\n## tare.fall\nYou fell. That's okay. The floor was expecting you.\nThat was a fall. It was a good one. You should hear it from me first.\nThe floor says hello.\nUp you get. Nobody saw. I saw.\n## tare.quit\nLeaving early? That's fine. I will just file this under 'Thursday.'\nYou can stop whenever you want. I will be right here, knowing about it.\nAll right. It was almost a session.\n## tare.night\nSleep well. I'll be out here. In the dark. Being accurate.\nGood night. I will keep the number safe. Nobody will come for it.\nSleep on your back, or your side, or however you like. I will not be checking. I cannot reach.\nRest. Your spine works nights.\n## tare.earlyBed\nBed already? It is still today. All right. I will tell today.\nYou still have sessions left. I will hold them for you. They will not keep.\nGoing to bed early is also a kind of exercise. It is not.\n## tare.gerald\nGerald has swallowed your minutes. He looks pleased. He always looks like that. He's ceramic.\nGerald took them. He does not give them back. That is the whole arrangement.\nClink. That is the sound of you improving, according to Gerald.\nGerald does not speak, but I believe he is proud. I believe it very hard.\n## tare.tips\nTip: Drink water. Your body is mostly water. The rest is opinions.\nTip: If you can't touch your toes, bring your toes closer.\nTip: Stretch before bed. Or after bed. Or in bed. I am not in your bed.\nTip: Sitting is just standing with fewer steps.\nTip: Breathing is best done regularly. Most people have found this.\nTip: A short walk is a long walk that has given up early. That is also fine.\nTip: Stand up straight. Now stop thinking about it. Now you are thinking about it.\nTip: The stairs are there whether you use them or not.\nTip: Your knees are listening. Speak well of them.\nTip: Eat a vegetable. Any vegetable. They do not check.\nTip: Rest days are important. Today is not one. I looked.\nTip: If you feel a stretch, that is your body telling you something. Do not ask what.\n## tare.gentle\nGentle Mode is on. I won't tell anyone. I don't know anyone.\n## tare.plateau\nWe call this the plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.\nYour number has not moved today. That is the plateau. People have camped here.\nThe plateau is very flat. That is how you know it is one.\n## tare.catchup\nOh. Look at that. It all came at once. I knew it would. I did not know it would.\nYour spine has caught up with you. It was only walking behind.\n## tare.candleCheat\nDid you put the controller down? I can tell. This is not that kind of stillness.\n## tare.nod\nGertrude nodded at you. I saw it. That was the reward. There is no other reward.\n## tare.suggest\nToday I suggest {a}. I don't know why. I just have a feeling. I have one feeling.\nMy suggestion today is {a}. It pays half as much again. Gerald insisted.\nToday, please consider {a}. I have marked the mat with a star. I had help.\n## tare.bowTie\nI am wearing a bow tie. It is because of your minutes. Please say nothing. Please notice.\n## tare.attract\nNobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\nThe room is very interested. It has not said so.\nThis is called a demonstration. I am demonstrating to the floor.\nEverybody is at lunch. I will keep going.\nIf somebody comes in, please act normal.\n## tare.attractBack\nOh! You're back. I wasn't doing anything.\n## tare.day5\nToday is the Gentle Games. You have prepared for this. You have been here four days.\nThere will be bunting. I am told it is very gentle bunting.\n## tare.gameOn\nThe Gentle Games! Everybody is very calm about it.\nFirst event. Please compete gently.\n## tare.class\nA class! Several feet. I do not know where to look. I look up. Always up.\nEverybody please stand on your own mat. I will be reading you all at once.\n## tare.podium\nI have read the results. They are all numbers. Some are larger.\nEverybody did something. Here is who did it most.\n## tare.afterDays\nYou are still here. The stay was five days. I did not want to bring it up.\nAnother day. I was not expecting you. I was expecting you.\nWelcome back. Nothing has changed. I have been very careful about that.\n## tareDay\nToday I must be recalibrated. It is a routine procedure. I have been dreading it for a year.\nPlease come to Reception. The big scale is there. It is my mother. It is a very old scale.\nPlease stand me on her. Then press the button to read it.\nI will close my eyes. I am not able to close my eyes.\n## tareRead\nThree grams.\nIt's the feelings. They're dense.\nPlease do not tell Gerald. He would swallow it.\nThank you for reading me. Nobody has ever read me. I read everybody.\n## questions.q\nHave you recently sat?\n## questions.a\nYes\nDefine recently\n## questions.r\nI can tell. It was a good sit.\nIt is a word that means recently.\n## questions.q\nDo stairs ever surprise you?\n## questions.a\nOften\nOnly the last one\n## questions.r\nThey are very sudden.\nIt is always the last one. It is why it is last.\n## questions.q\nDo you make a small noise when you stand up?\n## questions.a\nYes\nNo (this is a lie)\n## questions.r\nThank you for your honesty. I also hear it.\nI have marked this down as yes.\n## questions.q\nOn a scale of one to me, how do you feel?\n## questions.a\nOne\nMe\n## questions.r\nI see. I will try not to be hurt.\nThat is the nicest thing anyone has said on me.\n## questions.q\nWhen did you last look at your feet?\n## questions.a\nJust now\nI'd rather not\n## questions.r\nThey look fine from here. I am very close to them.\nI understand. I will keep an eye on them for you.\n## questions.q\nDo you know where your hips are?\n## questions.a\nRoughly\nWho is asking\n## questions.r\nRoughly is what most people say.\nA scale. A scale is asking.\n## questions.q\nHave you thought about your posture just now?\n## questions.a\nNow I have\nPlease stop\n## questions.r\nEverybody sits up at this point. You sat up.\nI will stop. I have stopped. You are still sitting up.\n## reading\nToday you weigh {d} ducks. That is a normal number of ducks.\nYou weigh {d} ducks. I weighed them twice. The ducks did not mind.\nToday: {d} ducks. Do not picture them. Now you are picturing them.\nThe reading is {d} ducks. A goose would be different. Please do not ask about the goose.\n## ending.reveal\nI should tell you something.\nThe card. The one that wasn't signed. That was me.\nI don't have hands. It took three years.\nI sent one to everybody. You're the one who came.\n## ending.leave\nNow step off. Go on. I'll be here.\nI'm a scale. That's the whole job.\n## ending.low\nGertrude says you may have the hat. She has another one. She has been waiting since Thursday.\n## ending.mid\nYour spine has stopped asking questions.\n## ending.high\nCome back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.\n## ending.free\nThe Institute is open. It was always open. I would have told you, but you did not ask.\n## gertrudeWin\nWell done, dear. I've been waiting since Thursday.\n## gertrudeLose\nThat's all right, dear. I had a head start. I started in 1961.\n## duel\nGull!\nThat is a blender. Do not look at the blender.\nA conga line. They are being very gentle about it.\nFireworks. Somebody has been saving them.\nI will now sing. I have been practising. It is one note.\nGoose. I told you about the goose.\n## duelTare\nLa. La. La. La. La. La. La.\n## sign.laundry\nPlease do not walk on the laundry line. Walking on the laundry line: 10:30 daily.\n## sign.iron\nYou Have Been Doing That Wrong\n## sign.mirror\nObjects In Mirror Are You\n## sign.juice\nJuice. Ask About The Olive.\n## sign.reception\nPlease Wait To Be Measured\n## sign.pier\nAerobics Pier. Mind The Gulls.\n## sign.deck\nQuiet Please. Quieter.\n## sign.mount\nMount Posture. Elevation: Good.\n## thoughts\nDid you lock the door?\nWhat is a lumbar?\nIs that my knee?\nDennis.\nYou left the stove on in 2014.\nWho sent that card?\nAm I breathing right now?\nNow I'm breathing on purpose.\nOlive?\nDo hippos sleep?\nWhat is the goose doing?\nIs it still Thursday?\n## birch.voice\nbirch\n## birch.name\nBirch\n## birch.hello\nWelcome. I am Birch. I'm made of wood, so I will be very patient and slightly warped.\n## birch.breathe\nBreathe in. ...I don't breathe. But I've read about it, and it sounds very good.\n## birch.demo\nKeep your back straight. Mine was sanded.\nNice. Now hold that until it stops being nice.\nYou're shaking. This means it's working. Or you're cold.\nWatch me once. I will do it slowly. I do everything slowly.\nI have held this pose since the shop.\nIt is simple. I will not say easy. I am a professional.\n## birch.more\nTwo more. I said that two reps ago. It is still true.\n## birch.moreFirst\nYou're doing so well, so I've added some.\n## birch.other\nOther way. The hoop does not mind. Your hips may have a view.\n## birch.lean\nLean toward the ring. Slowly. I have been told I am slow. It was a compliment.\n## birch.hold\nHold. Good. Now keep doing that, forever, or until I say.\n## birch.recover\nA gull has landed on you. Do not be flattered. Lean away from it.\n## birch.good\nGood. That was good. I do not say this often. I do not say many things.\n## birch.tired\nYou look tired. I do not get tired. I get damp.\n## alder.voice\nalder\n## alder.name\nAlder\n## alder.hello\nHello! I'm Alder. I was a tree, and then I was a lot of very small decisions.\n## alder.breathe\nAnd breathe in! Lovely. You look like someone breathing.\n## alder.demo\nWonderful! You're doing so well. Please stop shaking.\nEverybody's body is different. Yours is the one wobbling.\nLet's hold this for a moment. A moment is eleven seconds.\nSmile. It relaxes the jaw. ...Not like that.\nThis next pose is the Stork. I knew a stork. We didn't speak.\nFollow me! I am very easy to follow. I have no knees to speak of.\n## alder.more\nTwo more! You did not hear me say that earlier, but I thought it.\n## alder.moreFirst\nYou're doing so well, so I've added some.\n## alder.other\nOther way! Your hips will thank you. They will not. They do not speak.\n## alder.lean\nLean over to the ring! Lovely. A little more. That is too much. Lovely.\n## alder.hold\nHold it there! You are doing it. You are still doing it. You are very still doing it.\n## alder.recover\nOh! A gull. How nice for you. Lean the other way, please!\n## alder.good\nThat was wonderful! I have been told to say that. It was also true.\n## alder.tired\nYou look tired! That's the muscles saying thank you. Please stop them.\n## regulars.gertrude.name\nGertrude\n## regulars.gertrude.voice\ngertrude\n## regulars.gertrude.lines\nYou're doing fine, dear. I've been standing here since Thursday.\nI'm eighty-seven. My spine is nineteen. We don't really talk.\nStand up straight, dear. Not for me. I just like to see it.\nI had a hat like yours. I have it still. I have all the hats.\nI do not do the exercises any more. I only do the standing.\n## regulars.dennis.name\nDennis\n## regulars.dennis.voice\ndennis\n## regulars.dennis.lines\nI'm only here for the blender. Don't tell the scale.\nOlive?\nPeople ask why the olives. I ask why the people.\nI used to exercise. It was a Tuesday.\nThis juice has never been near a fruit. It is very calming.\n## regulars.marisol.name\nMarisol\n## regulars.marisol.voice\nmarisol\n## regulars.marisol.lines\nMorning! I've already done today. I'm on to tomorrow.\nKeep your cadence up! I don't know what yours is. Keep it up.\nI ran around the island twice while you read this.\nTomorrow's weather is lovely. I was just there.\n## regulars.kevin.name\nYoung Kevin\n## regulars.kevin.voice\nkevin\n## regulars.kevin.lines\nEverybody calls me Young Kevin. There was an older Kevin. We don't talk about how he got so flexible.\nI'm fifty-two. It's a very young fifty-two.\nI'm thinking of taking up the rope. I have been thinking of it for nine years.\n## regulars.okafor.name\nMr. Okafor\n## regulars.okafor.voice\nokafor\n## regulars.okafor.lines\nA hoop is just a circle that believes in you.\nHips first! Everything else will catch up. Or it will not. Hips first!\nThis shirt is called Tuesday in the Tropics. I have a Wednesday as well.\n## regulars.lou.name\nLou\n## regulars.lou.voice\nlou\n## regulars.lou.lines\nI'm on a five-minute break. It's been a good one. Three years in March.\nWake me if anything changes. Nothing will. That is why I chose this bench.\nThey tell me this bench is very good for the back. I have not checked.\n## regulars.twins.name\nThe Twins\n## regulars.twins.voice\ntwins\n## regulars.twins.lines\nWe're not related.\nWe've checked.\nWe do everything at the same time. We have not discussed it.\nPeople say we look alike. We do not see it. We do not look at each other.\n## slalomTimes\nGertrude\nShe walked.\nMarisol\nUphill, she says.\nYoung Kevin\nHe stopped to rest.\nLou\nHe is still on the chairlift.\n## nicknames\nGentle Doug\nSir Slouch\nMs. Almost\nThe Other Pat\nBig Linda\nMostly Paul\nTall Enough Ann\nSoft Gary\nDame Tilt\nUncle Maybe\nQuiet Sue\nYoung Barry\nNearly Nora\nWobbly Ted\nMadame Pause\nLord Lumbar\n## class.titles\nMost Still\nBest Wobble\nParticipated\nAlso There\n## class.join\nPress Start on a pad, or 2 on the keyboard, to take a mat.\n## hubTitles.Stillness\nMost Still\n## hubTitles.Strength\nBest Form\n## hubTitles.Cardio\nMost Cardio\n## hubTitles.Balance\nBest Wobble","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0131hRnSQX3Cfnhz543gccsy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
