{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UnmmVzL2SuzoJhZRySGNb2","type":"tool_result","content":"236\t**Tone rules.** Short sentences. Sincere, polite, a little too personal. Translated-instruction-manual cadence. No sarcasm, no meanness, no profanity, no pop-culture jokes, no references to being a game. Praise that wobbles. Facts nobody asked for. Tare is needy but never says so outright. Every text box: at most 2 lines of about 60 characters; a line is one thought. Use these lines verbatim and write as many more in the same voice as the game needs (aim for 150+ total, so a second playthrough still surprises). All text lives in `game/data/lines.js`.\n237\t\n238\t**Tare** (talking scale; \"tare\" is the button that zeroes one). A white slab with two soft footprints on top, a small dial, short legs, cyan LED eyes on the front edge and 8 faces (neutral, happy, worried, smug, shocked, sad, asleep, judging). Hops with squash and stretch. High, quick gibberish.\n239\t\n240\t- \"Oh! Feet. Good morning, feet.\"\n241\t- \"You came back. I wasn't worried. I was just standing here, on the floor, where I live.\"\n242\t- \"It has been one day since you last stepped on me. I counted it twice to be sure.\"\n243\t- \"Please stand still. Stiller. That was the wrong way.\"\n244\t- \"You lean beautifully. Like a tower people visit.\"\n245\t- \"You put more weight on your left foot. Your right foot has noticed.\"\n246\t- \"Your Spine Age is 58. That's younger than yesterday! Your spine has been through a lot.\"\n247\t- \"I am not allowed to say whether this is good. It is a number.\"\n248\t- \"You are my favorite. You are also my only.\"\n249\t- Long absence (real clock): \"It has been 9 days. I kept your spot warm. I am not able to generate heat.\"\n250\t- Paused 3 times: \"You paused. That's 3 times today. I'm not counting. Three.\"\n251\t- Idle on the island: \"Are you still there? I can feel you not standing on me.\"\n252\t- 0★: \"You finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\"\n253\t- 0★: \"That was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\"\n254\t- 1★: \"Good effort! I could tell it was effort.\"\n255\t- 2★: \"Well done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.\"\n256\t- 3★: \"You barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don't do that.\"\n257\t- Fall: \"You fell. That's okay. The floor was expecting you.\"\n258\t- Quit early: \"Leaving early? That's fine. I will just file this under 'Thursday.'\"\n259\t- Night: \"Sleep well. I'll be out here. In the dark. Being accurate.\"\n260\t- Gerald: \"Gerald has swallowed your minutes. He looks pleased. He always looks like that. He's ceramic.\"\n261\t- Tips: \"Tip: Drink water. Your body is mostly water. The rest is opinions.\" / \"Tip: If you can't touch your toes, bring your toes closer.\" / \"Tip: Stretch before bed. Or after bed. Or in bed. I am not in your bed.\" / \"Tip: Sitting is just standing with fewer steps.\"\n262\t\n263\t**The instructors** are wooden artists' mannequins: smooth egg heads, ball joints, no blinking, infinite patience. The player picks one on Day 1; they differ in voice, palette and lines.\n264\t\n265\t- **Birch** (oak tones, tall, deep slow voice): \"Welcome. I am Birch. I'm made of wood, so I will be very patient and slightly warped.\" / \"Breathe in. ...I don't breathe. But I've read about it, and it sounds very good.\" / \"Keep your back straight. Mine was sanded.\" / \"Nice. Now hold that until it stops being nice.\" / \"You're shaking. This means it's working. Or you're cold.\" / \"Two more. I said that two reps ago. It is still true.\"\n266\t- **Alder** (pale maple, carved ponytail, warm bright voice): \"Hello! I'm Alder. I was a tree, and then I was a lot of very small decisions.\" / \"Wonderful! You're doing so well. Please stop shaking.\" / \"Everybody's body is different. Yours is the one wobbling.\" / \"Let's hold this for a moment. A moment is eleven seconds.\" / \"Smile. It relaxes the jaw. ...Not like that.\" / \"This next pose is the Stork. I knew a stork. We didn't speak.\"\n267\t\n268\t**The Regulars** (chibi rigs, each with their own palette and voice pitch; they fill backgrounds, toss hoops, set times):\n269\t- **Gertrude**, 87, Spine Age 19, lilac tracksuit, sunhat, quavery: \"You're doing fine, dear. I've been standing here since Thursday.\" / \"I'm eighty-seven. My spine is nineteen. We don't really talk.\"\n270\t- **Dennis**, runs the Juice Bar, never exercises, holds a blender: \"I'm only here for the blender. Don't tell the scale.\" / \"Olive?\"\n271\t- **Marisol**, headband, always moving: \"Morning! I've already done today. I'm on to tomorrow.\"\n272\t- **Young Kevin**, 52: \"Everybody calls me Young Kevin. There was an older Kevin. We don't talk about how he got so flexible.\"\n273\t- **Mr. Okafor**, loud shirts: \"A hoop is just a circle that believes in you.\"\n274\t- **Lou**, on a bench (`Sleeping`): \"I'm on a five-minute break. It's been a good one. Three years in March.\"\n275\t- **The Twins**: \"We're not related.\" \"We've checked.\"\n276\t\n277\t**Candle thoughts:** \"Did you lock the door?\" / \"What is a lumbar?\" / \"Is that my knee?\" / \"Dennis.\" / \"You left the stove on in 2014.\" / \"Who sent that card?\" / \"Am I breathing right now?\" / \"Now I'm breathing on purpose.\" / \"Olive?\"\n278\t\n279\t**Boot messages:** Zeroing the scale / Sanding the instructors / Counting the ducks / Telling the hippo.\n280\t\n281\t---\n282\t\n283\t## 8. Art direction\n284\t\n285\tThe engine's native look (3D skeleton puppets drawn as crisp pixel art at `res: 'ps1', expand: true`, about 427 × 240 on 16:9) moved into bright daylight. ✔ It looks right: a white room, sea through a big window, pale wood floor, coral player, cyan accents.\n286\t\n287\t**Palette:** white `#f6fafa`, wall shade `#dfe9ea`, sky `#8fd3f4` → `#d8f3fb`, sea `#49b6c9` → `#2f97ad`, floor `#ecd9bd` → `#d9bd96`, UI accent `#2cc6e6`, ink `#20404c`, player coral `#ff7a59`, mint `#bfeee0`, oak `#d9b68a`, maple `#ecd3ac`. Colour never carries meaning alone (ring state also has shape and sound).\n288\t\n289\t**Scene recipe ✔:** paint directly on `r.ctx` first in `draw`, then queue actors. **In `brawler`, +y comes toward the camera** (lower on screen), despite what the card's table suggests: the back wall's base is `r.w(0, -44, 0)[1]`, mats sit near y = 0, floor boards run from y = -44 to y = 90. Shade with `E.mix` bands, keep the window as big as the wall. Character size: 2.1 for one rig, 1.9 for two, 1.5 for four. Scenes: `camera: { zoom: false }` on every fixed camera (the wheel belongs to Step Class).\n290\t\n291\t**Rooms (each needs 3 to 8 props and its own light):** Stillness Deck (open air, sea, wind chimes, ferns), Iron Room (white, mirror, comically small dumbbells, a water cooler, motivational signs: \"You Have Been Doing That Wrong\"), Pier (bunting, benches, gulls), Reception (Tare's mat, brochures), Juice Bar (blender, olives), Bungalow (bed, rail), Raft at dusk (lanterns).\n292\t\n293\t**Lights:** morning ambient about .92, noon lights off, dusk about .62 with warm lamps (`game.lights`). Keep bright scenes bright; a dark look is wrong here. Canvas lighting only: no `enableGPU`, and no WebGPU requirement for the hub.\n294\t\n295\t**Performance is not a goal.** Your brief treats the budget as unlimited, with frame rates and optimization out of scope: add the detail, crowd, particles and lights a scene wants, and don't spend time optimizing.\n296\t\n297\t**Draw these yourself (they make it feel like the source):** Tare; the mannequin joints; Gerald; the Plate; rings; yoga mats; step benches; tiny dumbbells; candle and flame; hoops; thought bubbles; tea tray, olives, glasses, gecko; ski gates, snowman; clothesline, pegs, socks, hamper; water cups; Member Cards. Generic props come from the engine's store: `node engine/tools/asset-find.mjs \"plant pot\"` (✔ benches, succulents, tubs, beds exist; no gym gear), read `engine/docs/ASSETS.md`, cut a set with `engine/tools/asset-set.mjs`. Pigeons and gulls are `E.Blob` with wings.\n298\t\n299\t**Title screen:** the studio, sea, Tare hopping on a mat, the logo with `E.font.title` at scale 3 to 4 in cyan. Keep clear of the corner buttons (top right 110 × 60 CSS px).\n300\t\n301\t---\n302\t\n303\t## 9. Animation recipes (all ✔)\n304\t\n305\tRigs are `E.Humanoid` (`weapon: null`). Player and Regulars `chibi`; instructors `build: 'heroic', limbW: 1.5, torsoW: 2.5, hair: 'bald'` (Alder `'ponytail'`) with every colour key in wood tones. Their ball joints: after `rig.draw`, in the same `r.actor`, for `kneeL kneeR elbowL elbowR shL shR`: `const w = rig.worldOffset(rig.J[k]), p = (rig.lastView || r.view).p(w[0], w[1], w[2]);` then `px.disc` radius 3 and radius 2 in two wood tones at `(ox + p[0], oy + p[1])`.\n306\t\n307\t**Real motion capture, including actual yoga, plays on these rigs.** Cut the small set in section 15. Then:\n308\t\n309\t```js\n310\tconst lib = Mocap.load(window.MOCAP.FITCLIPS);\n311\tfunction makeRig(opts) {\n312\t  const rig = new E.Humanoid(Object.assign({ weapon: null }, opts));\n313\t  Mocap.drive(rig, lib);              // first\n314\t  const base = rig.solvePose;         // then our layer: a hand-posed body, then the wobble\n315\t  rig.wob = [0, 0]; rig.body = null;\n316\t  rig.solvePose = function () {\n317\t    base.call(this);\n318\t    if (this.body) setBody(this, this.body(this));\n319\t    const [ax, ay] = this.wob; if (!ax && !ay) return;\n320\t    const J = this.J, a = ax * .45, b = ay * .3, ca = Math.cos(a), sa = Math.sin(a), cb = Math.cos(b), sb = Math.sin(b);\n321\t    for (const k in J) { if (k === 'bladeDir' || !J[k]) continue; const p = J[k];   // turn every joint about the feet\n322\t      const r2 = p[1] * ca + p[2] * sa, z2 = -p[1] * sa + p[2] * ca, f2 = p[0] * cb + z2 * sb, z3 = -p[0] * sb + z2 * cb;\n323\t      p[0] = f2; p[1] = r2; p[2] = Math.max(z3, 0); }\n324\t  };\n325\t  return rig;\n326\t}\n327\t// each step. A clip turns the rig by its own heading, so aim with tgt minus that turn:\n328\trig.wob = [p.x, p.y];  rig.mocap = lib.sample(clip, t);   // rig.mocap = null to stop\n329\trig.update(dt, { x, y, z: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, facing: tgt - (rig.spin || 0) });\n330\t```\n331\t\n332\tFacing: π/2 looks at the camera; 0 is profile. **To hold a pose,** sample inside its window and drift slowly: `t = a + (b - a) * .3 * (.5 + .5 * Math.sin(time * .7))`. Clip motion keeps it alive.\n333\t\n334\t**Pose table** (windows ✔ seen on contact sheets; stork, triangle and dog ✔ seen in the studio):\n335\t\n336\t| Pose | Clip | Window (s) | `tgt` |\n337\t|---|---|---|---|\n338\t| Stork (one leg, arms wide) | `111_39_part1` | 3.6 to 7.0 | 1.57 |\n339\t| Knee Lift | `111_39_part2` | .5 to 2.4 | 1.57 |\n340\t| Triangle | `111_39_part3` | 2.2 to 5.2 | 1.2 |\n341\t| Warrior (wide stance, arms wide) | `111_39_part3` | 6.6 to 7.6 | 1.57 |\n342\t| Low Lunge | `111_38_part1` | 2.9 to 5.0 | .25 |\n343\t| Down Dog | `111_38_part2` | 2.8 to 5.2 | .25 |\n344\t| Forward Fold | `111_38_part2` | 8.0 to 8.8 | .25 |\n345\t| Low Plank | `111_41_part3` | 3.4 to 6.4 | .25 |\n346\t\n347\tOther clips in the set: `Meditate` (Candle), `Pushup`, `22_14`, `Jumping Jacks`, `Run_Loop`, `Walk_Loop`, `Hop_One_Foot_Loop` (regaining balance), `Dizzy` (stumble), `Get_Up_From_Back` (falls), `Victory`, `Cheering_Two_Hands` (3★), `Stretch_Yawn` (morning), `Sleeping` (Lou, bed), `Greeting` (instructor's bow), `Wave_Hello`, `Waiting_Loop`, `Idle_Subtle` (Regulars). Crossfade with `lib.blend(a, b, k)`, or fade a clip over the rig with `rig.mocapW`.\n348\t\n349\t**Moves with no clip: pose the body yourself.** You set hips, feet, hands; IK does knees and elbows:\n350\t\n351\t```js\n352\tconst { V3 } = E;  // V3.add, V3.mul, V3.norm\n353\tfunction setBody(rig, b) {\n354\t  const o = rig.o, J = rig.J, hipC = b.hip;\n355\t  J.hipC = hipC; J.hipL = V3.add(hipC, [0, -o.hipHalf, 0]); J.hipR = V3.add(hipC, [0, o.hipHalf, 0]);\n356\t  for (const s of [-1, 1]) { const hip = s > 0 ? J.hipR : J.hipL, foot = s > 0 ? b.footR : b.footL,\n357\t      [kn, f2] = E.ik3(hip, foot, o.legUpper, o.legLower, b.knee ? b.knee(s) : [1, s * .3, .1]);\n358\t    J[s > 0 ? 'kneeR' : 'kneeL'] = kn; J[s > 0 ? 'footR' : 'footL'] = f2; }\n359\t  const dir = V3.norm(b.chest || [0, 0, 1]), shC = V3.add(hipC, V3.mul(dir, o.torso)); J.shC = shC;\n360\t  J.shL = V3.add(shC, [0, -o.shoulderHalf, 0]); J.shR = V3.add(shC, [0, o.shoulderHalf, 0]);\n361\t  J.head = V3.add(shC, V3.mul(V3.norm([dir[0], dir[1], dir[2] + .4]), o.neck + o.headR));\n362\t  for (const s of [-1, 1]) { const sh = s > 0 ? J.shR : J.shL, hand = s > 0 ? b.handR(shC, sh) : b.handL(shC, sh),\n363\t      [el, h2] = E.ik3(sh, hand, o.armUpper, o.armLower, [-1, s * .7, -.2]);\n364\t    J[s > 0 ? 'elbowR' : 'elbowL'] = el; J[s > 0 ? 'handR' : 'handL'] = h2; }\n365\t}\n366\tconst add = V3.add;\n367\tconst sideLunge = u => rig => { const o = rig.o, a = Math.abs(u), w = o.footSpread + 5.4;   // feet stay down at full stretch\n368\t  return { hip: [0, u * 3.8, o.hipZ - a * o.hipZ * .4], footL: [.5, -w, 0], footR: [.5, w, 0], knee: s => [1, s * .7, .1],\n369\t    chest: [.28 * a, -u * .1, 1], handL: c => add(c, [4, -.6, -2.6]), handR: c => add(c, [4, .6, -2.6]) }; };\n370\tconst hula = ph => rig => { const o = rig.o, hx = Math.cos(ph) * 2.1, hy = Math.sin(ph) * 2.1;\n371\t  return { hip: [hx, hy, o.hipZ - .5], footL: [.3, -o.footSpread - 1, 0], footR: [.3, o.footSpread + 1, 0], chest: [-hx * .22, -hy * .22, 1],\n372\t    handL: (c, sh) => add(sh, [.4, -6, 1.6 + Math.sin(ph) * .6]), handR: (c, sh) => add(sh, [.4, 6, 1.6 - Math.sin(ph) * .6]) }; };\n373\tconst stepUp = (k, zb = 5) => rig => { const o = rig.o;   // k 0..1: up onto a bench zb high\n374\t  return { hip: [.2 + k * 1.2, k * 1.6, o.hipZ + k * zb * .7], footL: [k > .5 ? 3 : -1, -o.footSpread, k > .85 ? zb : 0], footR: [3, o.footSpread, zb * Math.min(1, k * 2)],\n375\t    chest: [.1, 0, 1], handL: (c, sh) => add(sh, [1 + k * 3, -1.2, -3 + k * 2]), handR: (c, sh) => add(sh, [3 - k * 3, 1.2, -1 - k * 2]) }; };\n376\t```\n377\t\n378\tSet `rig.body = sideLunge(u)` each step (`rig.body = null` to release). Walking on the rope uses the rig's own walk plus arms held out the same way. Faces: `expr: 'smile' | 'wince'` in `rig.update`. Tare and Gerald are hand-drawn with `px` in `r.queue`, with a spring for squash; Tare's portrait is a function passed to `E.Dialog`. Check motion with `node engine/tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n379\t\n380\t---\n381\t\n382\t## 10. Audio (all from code, no files)\n383\t\n384\t**Music is 10% by default.** ✔ `menu: { settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }] }` sets `game.settings.music` and `audio.musicVolume` to .1. Never compensate by raising track volumes.\n385\t\n386\t**Songs:** original, gentle, a bit too pleasant; think hold music in a very clean building. Step notation with `sine`, `triangle`, soft `pulse`, sparse `drums`; use a track's `vol`, `gate`, `vib`, `name`, `on` and `audio.layer` to add parts as you do well. Write about 12: studio, island (morning), island (dusk), yoga pad, iron, step A (100 bpm), step B (120 bpm), jog, ski, tray lounge, laundry pizzicato, festival, ending, plus jingles (star 1/2/3, unlock, day done) via `audio.sting`. Do not reuse the engine's songbook as your soundtrack, and imitate nothing.\n387\t\n388\t**SFX** via `audio.define`: Tare's signature two-note step-on boop, creak, in-ring chime that climbs, stumble, hippo clink, gull, pigeon flurry, flame flick, hoop whirr (pitch follows speed), ski carve (noise), tray clink, olive plop, rope creak, star stamps, menu tick and confirm. The Stork tier 2 balance tone is your own oscillator on `audio.bus('sfx')`.\n389\t\n390\t**Voices: Animalese-style gibberish, a sound per letter, on the voice bus.** `new E.Dialog(game, { voice: (ch, i, talk) => babble(talk.name, ch) })` (`talk.name` is the speaker the current `say` gave). `babble` makes a 60 to 90 ms oscillator (sine or triangle) through a band-pass filter on `audio.ctx`, connected to `audio.bus('voice')`, with pitch and filter from a table by letter (vowels open and longer, consonants short), skipping spaces and punctuation. Each speaker has base pitch, speed, wave and vibrato: Tare high and quick, Birch low and slow, Alder warm, Gertrude quavery, and so on. Guard for `audio.ctx` being null (headless, or before the first input). Add a `voice` slider setting that applies `audio.voiceVolume`. Exercise grunts use the same function.\n391\t\n392\t---\n393\t\n394\t## 11. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\n395\t\n396\t**Rules:** at most 6 choices on a screen; one idea per screen; no tables or data grids anywhere; body text never below font scale 1 (`font: 'tiny'` is banned), key numbers scale 2 to 3; anchor everything to `r.W` / `r.H` with 12 px margins; ✔ judge it from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n397\t\n398\t**Canvas UI, bright and round.** `E.Menu`'s default is a dark JRPG window: wrong here. Write one **`Pills`** widget (about 70 lines) and use it on every game screen: white rounded pills, cyan focus that grows slightly, soft tick on move. Up/down (or left/right) with `input.repeat`, ✕ or Enter picks, ○ backs out. **Mouse: hover moves focus, a click picks** (`input.pointer()`, `input.clicked()`). `E.Dialog` takes `{ bg: ['#ffffff', '#eaf6f8'], border: '#2cc6e6', color: '#20404c', nameColor: '#14a8c8' }`, but it hard-codes a near-black text shadow that smears on white. **Make this one engine change ✔:** in `class Dialog` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, replace each `shadow: '#05040a'` used for the name, the text and the choices (3 places, around lines 9153 to 9176) with `shadow: this.shadow === undefined ? '#05040a' : this.shadow`, then set `talk.shadow = null`.\n399\t\n400\t**Prompts** come only from one `prompt(action, verb)` helper that draws a chip at bottom right, showing what the player used last. Controller: `input.label(action)` gives ✕ ○ □ △ L1 R1 L2 R2 Options ✔ (the pixel font draws them all). Keyboard and mouse: `input.label(a, 'keyboard') + ' / ' + input.label(a, 'mouse')`, e.g. \"Space / Left click\". Lean's own prompt says \"Left stick\" / \"WASD\" / \"Move the mouse\" by the live source. ✔ `menu: { settings: [{ key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation' }] }` defaults to PlayStation, and the standard Settings → Controller → Button symbols offers Xbox (A B X Y).\n401\t\n402\t**Standard screens stay the engine's** (pause, settings, controls, rebinding, full screen, boot). ✔ Theme and fix them:\n403\t\n404\t```js\n405\tnew E.Shell(game, { theme: { ink: '#20404c', paper: '#f7fbfb', accent: '#14a8c8', muted: '#5f7f8a', danger: '#e0553a', line: '#c8dde2', font: 'system-ui, sans-serif', titleFont: 'system-ui, sans-serif' } });\n406\t// the engine's HTML menus don't move focus on hover. This makes them:\n407\tif (typeof document !== 'undefined') document.addEventListener('pointerover', e => {\n408\t  const b = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('.esh-sh button:not(:disabled), .esh-sh input:not(:disabled)');\n409\t  if (b && e.pointerType === 'mouse') b.focus({ preventScroll: true }); });\n410\t```\n411\t```css\n412\t@media (min-height:700px){.esh-mod{zoom:1.5}} @media (min-height:1000px){.esh-mod{zoom:2}}   /* readable at 10 feet */\n413\t.esh button:focus,.esh input:focus{outline:3px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}\n414\t[data-sys=need]{background:rgba(5,3,12,.35)!important;align-items:flex-end!important}          /* lets attract show through */\n415\t```\n416\t\n417\t**Game settings** (`menu.settings`): `music` .1, `glyphs`, `voice` slider, Gentle Mode, Breath Hold/Toggle, Tare's Tips on/off. `menu.items`: Restart Session, Dev Mode. `menu.quit: 'title'`, autosaving first. `menu.controls` names the actions in plain words and hides the ones a player has no reason to rebind.\n418\t\n419\t**Touch-only devices.** ✔ `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })` shows exactly \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button and no touch controls; the CSS above lets the attract mode show behind it. Attract runs after 10 s as usual (taps produce no actions, so it stays running).\n420\t\n421\t**Comfort:** use `game.shake` / `game.flash`, which follow the settings. Pausing is standard; every activity scene is `pausable: true`.\n422\t\n423\t**About / Credits screen** (from Title): paged, big text, no scrolling wall. Pages: Source Information (every field your brief lists, in its order), Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, Credits (engine; Mesh2Motion and Quaternius, CC0; CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database; asset store sources). `build.mjs` injects your exit-interview JSON into the page as `G.ABOUT`, so screen, file and chat reply cannot disagree. Usage shows \"added on import\" as your brief says.\n424\t\n425\t---\n426\t\n427\t## 12. Attract Mode\n428\t\n429\tAfter **10 s with no input** on the title or any top-level menu (`game.hook('input', ...)`: `anyPressed`, stick, pointer movement). **Any input** returns to the title and swallows the press (`input.consumeAll()`).\n430\t\n431\tFiction: nobody's here, so Tare shows the empty room around. A \"DEMO\" chip, the logo in a corner, \"Press any button\" (by device), and subtitled lines: \"Nobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\" On exit: \"Oh! You're back. I wasn't doing anything.\"\n432\t\n433\t**Playlist, about 15 s each, looping:** Island walk → Body Check → Stork Stand → Sun Flow → Quiet Candle → Squat Rail → Push-Up → Side Lunge → Step Class → Hoop Hips → Coastal Jog → Slalom → Tray Service → Laundry Line → four-mat Class → results with Gerald's coins → Grand Stillness. Each runs the real activity scene with the expert bot filling `intent`, with cheats allowed (no stumbles). It never touches saves or unlocks. Use a Regular's rig as the star.\n434\t\n435\t---\n436\t\n437\t## 13. Dev Mode\n438\t\n439\tReachable from the pause menu (`menu.items`), in every scene, on every device. It closes the pause and docks a canvas panel on the left third **while the game keeps running**, so balance changes are felt live. D-pad up/down moves, left/right adjusts (held accelerates, L1/R1 coarse), ✕ activates, ○ closes. Arrows on keyboard (WASD keeps leaning). Mouse: drag sliders; the pointer over the panel does not lean.\n440\t\n441\t**Live sliders** (all in one `DEV` object with defaults; \"Reset to defaults\" restores it; each shows default vs current):\n442\t- Lean: `k c s A nf`, ring scale, push strength, stumble threshold, mouse reach, nudge rate\n443\t- Scoring: star thresholds, rep tolerance, rhythm window scale, fatigue amount\n444\t- Cardio: hoop band, jog cadence band, jog speed\n445\t- Games: slalom speed and turn, tray gravity and friction, rope instability, gust strength\n446\t- World: time scale (0, .25, .5, 1, 2), minutes multiplier\n447\t\n448\t**Tools:** jump to any scene/activity/tier/day; finish now with N stars; unlock all; +10 minutes; set Spine Age; reset this member; no stumbles; bot plays (poor/average/good/expert); show Plate trace and numbers; frame step; force attract; **Pose Viewer** (pick any clip, scrub, print a pose row for `game/data/poses.js`); log `game.debug.snapshot()` to the console. Hidden in a hub session.\n449\t\n450\t---\n451\t\n452\t## 14. Multiplayer\n453\t\n454\t**Class (local, on its own, 2 to 4).** From the title: join with Start on a free pad or 2 on the keyboard (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`; `game.players[i]` has the same input API; keyboard players get `E.Input.halfKeys`). ✔ Half a keyboard runs out of keys with the full `INPUT` (the step and pace actions get none), so the Class scene sets its own `input`: the moves and menu actions plus `breath`, `catchL`, `catchR` only (left half F G H, right half `. / ,`), and its Step Class reads `lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right']`. Everyone gets a mat, a colour (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) and a pre-made rig, on one fixed screen at size 1.5 with a small Plate under each. Activities: Stork Stand, Quiet Candle, Squat Rail, Step Class (two lanes), Hoop Hips, 35 s each, or \"Surprise me\" (3 rounds). So every class-capable activity takes a list of **contestants** from the start, not one player. Scores are 0 to 1000 (`round(pct × 1000)`). Results: podium with polite titles (Most Still, Best Wobble, Participated). Tare reads them. Empty mats hold Regulars driven by bots, for life, not for score.\n455\t\n456\t**AI Hub session (`ghost` mode, 1 to 4).** Follow the protocol README (`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`); it is short, read it. Outside a session the game is unaffected and `connect()` answers `null`. ✔ This exact shape passed the harness at 1, 2, 3 and 4 players, on the bad network, and with the host leaving.\n457\t\n458\t**The round: \"Morning Class\".** Everyone plays the same 3 events on their own copy, in lockstep, seeing others as translucent seat-coloured ghosts on neighbouring mats (or in the world for Slalom and Jog). About 150 s: each event is 5 s intro + 40 s play + 5 s scores. Deal with `AIHub.rng('deal')`: one from Stork/Candle/Squat/Push-Up, one from Step/Hoop, one from Slalom/Jog.\n459\t\n460\t```js\n461\tconst inSession = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\n462\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', id: 'GAMEID', res: 'ps1', expand: true, touch: 'never', input: INPUT,\n463\t  autoPause: !inSession, live: inSession, fullscreen: inSession ? false : 'button',\n464\t  menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', items: inSession ? [] : [/* Restart, Dev Mode */], settings: [/* section 11 */] } });\n465\tgame.start({ scenes, scene: inSession ? 'round' : 'title', boot: {/* steps */} });\n466\tif (inSession) (async () => {\n467\t  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n468\t  if (!info) return game.go('title');\n469\t  AIHub.on('card', c => { card = c; });\n470\t  AIHub.on('start', () => {});\n471\t  AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => { /* ghost state */ });\n472\t  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { /* remove that ghost */ });\n473\t  AIHub.on('time-up', () => report());                  // result() at once if not reported\n474\t  AIHub.on('end', () => { over = true; game.audio.stopMusic(); game.audio.mute(true); game.input.clear(); });\n475\t  await game.booted; AIHub.ready();                     // no key press\n476\t})();\n477\t```\n478\t\n479\t- **Card (yours, `card: true`):** the studio with the players lined up on mats, Tare hopping, the title, each player's name and colour with a ready tick, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left. While `AIHub.time() === -Infinity`: `confirm` or `start` → `AIHub.answer('ready')`, `more` (△) → `AIHub.answer('more')`, clicks on Ready/More too. No menus or choices on the card. Show \"More time\" state from the `card` event (`asked`, `paused`).\n480\t- **Clock:** all event timing comes from `AIHub.time()`, not `game.time`. A frame over 50 ms gives up its time, so a slow machine's game clock lags and would desync. Countdown while negative. Play at ≥ 0. If `info.limitMs` is shorter than the round, shrink the events.\n481\t- **Randomness:** every activity takes its disturbances from `AIHub.rng('e' + eventIndex)` (and a seeded `E.rng` offline). `Math.random` is only for cosmetics like particles and blinks, because copies draw it at different rates.\n482\t- **Ghost data:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', a: eventIndex, l: [x, y], p: phase, w: [wx, wy], s: score }, { reliable: false })` about 10 times a second. Draw only if `a` matches your current event. `r.actor(..., { alpha: .5 })`, name tag in seat colour. Names come from `info.players`, drawn with `E.font` only (never HTML). Limit: 20 messages/s.\n483\t- **Reporting:** `AIHub.progress({ score: total, label: total + ' pts' })` about once a second; at the end `AIHub.result({ score: total, stats: { Steadiness: '84%' }, awards: [{ title: 'Most Still', detail: '...' }] })` once.\n484\t- **In a session:** no title, attract, dev, quit, restart or saved progress. Options opens the settings over the running round (`live`). No chat, emotes or custom names. No other network. Engine already ignores Options while Create is held ✔.\n485\t\n486\t**Head tags (`build.mjs` writes them), in this order ✔:**\n487\t\n488\t```html\n489\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n490\t<script>/* vendor/session.js, unmodified, first script in head */</script>\n491\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n492\t<title>THE TITLE — a tagline</title>\n493\t<meta name=\"description\" content=\"one or two sentences\">\n494\t<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#2cc6e6\">\n495\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\"><meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Wii Fit\">\n496\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n497\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n498\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Stay steadiest over 3 exercises; most points wins\">\n499\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse. Breathe: R2, Space or click\">\n500\t```\n501\t\n502\t---\n503\t\n504\t## 15. Tech and setup\n505\t\n506\t**Stack:** the my-3D2dge full engine (2D views), its `mode7`, `road`, `physics`, `rhythm` modules (all inside `my-3d2dge.js`), `Mocap` and a cut clip set, the hub client. No World3D, no other libraries. **Start from no single kit:** this game mixes genres, so use the full engine with your own page, and read `engine/kits/road.js`, `kart.js`, `rhythm.js`, `pinball.js` (physics) and `sports.js` (joining players) when you build those parts.\n507\t\n508\t**Fetch (✔ every command run from a clean folder; run from the dev folder):**\n509\t\n510\t```sh\n511\tgit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git _src\n512\tgit -C _src sparse-checkout set dist/handoff\n513\tcp -r _src/dist/handoff engine        # then remove _src\n514\tnpm install playwright@1.63.0         # uses the browsers already here. Never `playwright install`, whatever the engine's README says\n515\t\n516\tmkdir -p vendor/clipsrc/tools vendor/clipsrc/src/mocap tests/hub\n517\tB=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main\n518\tH=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub\n519\tcurl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/tools/anim-set.mjs $B/tools/anim-set.mjs\n520\tcurl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/tools/mocap-lib.mjs $B/tools/mocap-lib.mjs\n521\tcurl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/src/mocap/readable.js $B/src/mocap/readable.js    # the tool needs it exactly here\n522\tcurl -fsSLo vendor/readable.js $B/src/mocap/readable.js\n523\tcurl -fsSLo vendor/mocap.js $B/src/mocap/mocap.js\n524\tfor f in src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js src/mocap/sets/cmu.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_111.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_22.js; do curl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/$(basename $f) $B/$f; done\n525\tcurl -fsSLo vendor/session.js $H/session.js\n526\tfor f in harness.html bridge.js round.js; do curl -fsSLo tests/hub/$f $H/$f; done\n527\tnode vendor/clipsrc/tools/anim-set.mjs vendor/clipsrc/mesh2motion.js vendor/clipsrc/cmu.js vendor/clipsrc/CMU_111.js vendor/clipsrc/CMU_22.js \\\n528\t  --clips \"Pushup,Meditate,Jumping Jacks,Sleeping,Victory,Cheering_Two_Hands,Dizzy,Idle_Subtle,Greeting,CMU:Run_Loop,CMU:Walk_Loop,Stretch_Yawn,Get_Up_From_Back,Waiting_Loop,Hop_One_Foot_Loop,Wave_Hello,111_38_part1,111_38_part2,111_39_part1,111_39_part2,111_39_part3,111_41_part3,22_14\" \\\n529\t  --name FITCLIPS --out vendor/fitclips.js --credit \"Mesh2Motion (CC0), Quaternius (CC0), CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses)\"\n530\t# prints 23 clips, about 173 KB. vendor/clipsrc can then go; it is not bundled\n531\t```\n532\t\n533\tMore clips, if you want them: search `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/src/mocap/catalogs/cmu-takes.tsv` (take `NN_xx` lives in `examples/cmu-lib/CMU_NN.js`) and `.../catalogs/mesh2motion.json`.\n534\t\n535\t**Layout:**\n536\t\n537\t```\n538\tengine/        the handoff copy (my-3d2dge.js is the engine; API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md, tools/, kits/, docs/)\n539\tvendor/        readable.js, mocap.js, fitclips.js, session.js\n540\tgame/\n541\t  index.html   dev page: canvas (#screen with CSS width and height 100%, or it draws at 300×150 ✔) and the scripts in order\n542\t  core.js      G namespace, game, INPUT, DEV defaults, state, saves, deep links (#hub, #act/stork/1, #day/3, #ending)\n543\t  balance.js   Balance model, intent sources (devices, bots), Plate\n544\t  rigs.js      makeRig, setBody and moves, Tare, Gerald, joints, cast\n545\t  ui.js        Pills, prompt, Card, Results, DevPanel\n546\t  audio.js     songs, sfx, babble\n547\t  data/        lines.js, poses.js, activities.js, charts.js, courses.js, trays.js, days.js, unlocks.js\n548\t  activities/  hold.js, candle.js, rep.js, step.js, hoop.js, jog.js, slalom.js, tray.js, laundry.js\n549\t  scenes/      title, attract, member, arrival, island, bodycheck, session, evening, games, ending, about, class, round\n550\ttests/run.mjs  the one test command; tests/hub/ the harness\n551\tbuild.mjs      the one build command\n552\t```\n553\t\n554\tPlain scripts on one global `G`, no ES modules (the page must work from `file://`). **Build out by data:** a designer adds a tier, pose, chart, gate course, tray, line or day by editing `game/data/`, with no code change. Add a short `game/data/README.md` saying how.\n555\t\n556\t**Activity registry:**\n557\t\n558\t```js\n559\tG.activity({ id: 'stork', family: 'hold', discipline: 'Stillness', name: 'Stork Stand', view: 'brawler', camera: { zoom: false },\n560\t  class: true, hub: true, tiers: [ {/* numbers */}, {/* numbers */} ], stars: [.35, .65, .90], lines: {/* ... */},\n561\t  setup(ctx) {}, update(dt, ctx) {}, draw(r, ctx) {}, hud(r, ctx) {},\n562\t  result(ctx) { return { pct, detail }; },\n563\t  bot(ctx, skill) { return intent; },\n564\t  ghost(ctx) { return state; }, drawGhost(r, ctx, id, state) {} });\n565\t```\n566\t`ctx`: `{ tier, rng (seeded), contestants: [{ intent, bal, rig, name, color, score, local }], time, done, cheat }`. Every activity becomes its own pausable scene, generated from the entry. Set `game.debug = { snapshot() { return { scene, activity, tier, day, session, pct, stars, minutes, spineAge, lean, source }; } }`: tests and engine tools read it.\n567\t\n568\t**`build.mjs`:** concatenates engine, `vendor/readable.js`, `vendor/mocap.js`, `vendor/fitclips.js`, game files; replaces every `</script` with `<\\/script` in everything it inlines ✔; writes head tags, CSS, the boot markup at the start of `<body>` (copy the `e3-boot` div from `engine/game/index.html`); injects the exit-interview JSON as `G.ABOUT`; writes the single file to the place your brief names (pass it as an argument) and copies it to `tests/hub/game.html`. External CDN is allowed but not needed: inline everything. About 1.5 MB.\n569\t\n570\t**Engine changes:** only the small Dialog shadow patch (section 11) is required. Everything else works through the public API and the wrappers above. Note whatever you change, and why, for your Engine Feedback.\n571\t\n572\t**Traps already found (so you don't lose time on them):**\n573\t1. A custom `input` map replaces the preset (section 3).\n574\t2. `brawler`: +y is toward the camera (section 8).\n575\t3. Mouse movement doesn't change `lastDevice` from `'keyboard'` (section 3).\n576\t4. Default `music` is .5 and `glyphs` 'auto': set both (section 11).\n577\t5. Music at 10% hides the beat: click on the sfx bus (section 4).\n578\t6. HTML menus lack hover focus; the touch notice is 88% opaque (section 11).\n579\t7. `E.Dialog` hard-codes a dark text shadow (section 11). The standard Settings list is long at 10 feet: rely on its scrolling focus and the zoom CSS.\n580\t8. In tests, `game.fadeTime = 0`; `game.go` otherwise delays the new scene .22 s.\n581\t9. A frame past 50 ms gives up its time: browser tests here are software-rendered and slow, so wait on game state, never on the clock.\n582\t10. In Python Playwright use `page.wait_for_timeout`, not `time.sleep` (it freezes the event loop and frames never appear).\n583\t11. `E.store` is shared by id; set `id` on the game, and `E.store.clear()` between test games in one process.\n584\t12. Fixed-camera scenes need `camera: { zoom: false }`, or the wheel zooms instead of stepping.\n585\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"4dd6140f-bdea-4318-8585-fcb3d40d7766","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:23:12.409Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221037__x61bd7e/work/PLAN.md","content":"**Tone rules.** Short sentences. Sincere, polite, a little too personal. Translated-instruction-manual cadence. No sarcasm, no meanness, no profanity, no pop-culture jokes, no references to being a game. Praise that wobbles. Facts nobody asked for. Tare is needy but never says so outright. Every text box: at most 2 lines of about 60 characters; a line is one thought. Use these lines verbatim and write as many more in the same voice as the game needs (aim for 150+ total, so a second playthrough still surprises). All text lives in `game/data/lines.js`.\n\n**Tare** (talking scale; \"tare\" is the button that zeroes one). A white slab with two soft footprints on top, a small dial, short legs, cyan LED eyes on the front edge and 8 faces (neutral, happy, worried, smug, shocked, sad, asleep, judging). Hops with squash and stretch. High, quick gibberish.\n\n- \"Oh! Feet. Good morning, feet.\"\n- \"You came back. I wasn't worried. I was just standing here, on the floor, where I live.\"\n- \"It has been one day since you last stepped on me. I counted it twice to be sure.\"\n- \"Please stand still. Stiller. That was the wrong way.\"\n- \"You lean beautifully. Like a tower people visit.\"\n- \"You put more weight on your left foot. Your right foot has noticed.\"\n- \"Your Spine Age is 58. That's younger than yesterday! Your spine has been through a lot.\"\n- \"I am not allowed to say whether this is good. It is a number.\"\n- \"You are my favorite. You are also my only.\"\n- Long absence (real clock): \"It has been 9 days. I kept your spot warm. I am not able to generate heat.\"\n- Paused 3 times: \"You paused. That's 3 times today. I'm not counting. Three.\"\n- Idle on the island: \"Are you still there? I can feel you not standing on me.\"\n- 0★: \"You finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\"\n- 0★: \"That was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\"\n- 1★: \"Good effort! I could tell it was effort.\"\n- 2★: \"Well done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.\"\n- 3★: \"You barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don't do that.\"\n- Fall: \"You fell. That's okay. The floor was expecting you.\"\n- Quit early: \"Leaving early? That's fine. I will just file this under 'Thursday.'\"\n- Night: \"Sleep well. I'll be out here. In the dark. Being accurate.\"\n- Gerald: \"Gerald has swallowed your minutes. He looks pleased. He always looks like that. He's ceramic.\"\n- Tips: \"Tip: Drink water. Your body is mostly water. The rest is opinions.\" / \"Tip: If you can't touch your toes, bring your toes closer.\" / \"Tip: Stretch before bed. Or after bed. Or in bed. I am not in your bed.\" / \"Tip: Sitting is just standing with fewer steps.\"\n\n**The instructors** are wooden artists' mannequins: smooth egg heads, ball joints, no blinking, infinite patience. The player picks one on Day 1; they differ in voice, palette and lines.\n\n- **Birch** (oak tones, tall, deep slow voice): \"Welcome. I am Birch. I'm made of wood, so I will be very patient and slightly warped.\" / \"Breathe in. ...I don't breathe. But I've read about it, and it sounds very good.\" / \"Keep your back straight. Mine was sanded.\" / \"Nice. Now hold that until it stops being nice.\" / \"You're shaking. This means it's working. Or you're cold.\" / \"Two more. I said that two reps ago. It is still true.\"\n- **Alder** (pale maple, carved ponytail, warm bright voice): \"Hello! I'm Alder. I was a tree, and then I was a lot of very small decisions.\" / \"Wonderful! You're doing so well. Please stop shaking.\" / \"Everybody's body is different. Yours is the one wobbling.\" / \"Let's hold this for a moment. A moment is eleven seconds.\" / \"Smile. It relaxes the jaw. ...Not like that.\" / \"This next pose is the Stork. I knew a stork. We didn't speak.\"\n\n**The Regulars** (chibi rigs, each with their own palette and voice pitch; they fill backgrounds, toss hoops, set times):\n- **Gertrude**, 87, Spine Age 19, lilac tracksuit, sunhat, quavery: \"You're doing fine, dear. I've been standing here since Thursday.\" / \"I'm eighty-seven. My spine is nineteen. We don't really talk.\"\n- **Dennis**, runs the Juice Bar, never exercises, holds a blender: \"I'm only here for the blender. Don't tell the scale.\" / \"Olive?\"\n- **Marisol**, headband, always moving: \"Morning! I've already done today. I'm on to tomorrow.\"\n- **Young Kevin**, 52: \"Everybody calls me Young Kevin. There was an older Kevin. We don't talk about how he got so flexible.\"\n- **Mr. Okafor**, loud shirts: \"A hoop is just a circle that believes in you.\"\n- **Lou**, on a bench (`Sleeping`): \"I'm on a five-minute break. It's been a good one. Three years in March.\"\n- **The Twins**: \"We're not related.\" \"We've checked.\"\n\n**Candle thoughts:** \"Did you lock the door?\" / \"What is a lumbar?\" / \"Is that my knee?\" / \"Dennis.\" / \"You left the stove on in 2014.\" / \"Who sent that card?\" / \"Am I breathing right now?\" / \"Now I'm breathing on purpose.\" / \"Olive?\"\n\n**Boot messages:** Zeroing the scale / Sanding the instructors / Counting the ducks / Telling the hippo.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Art direction\n\nThe engine's native look (3D skeleton puppets drawn as crisp pixel art at `res: 'ps1', expand: true`, about 427 × 240 on 16:9) moved into bright daylight. ✔ It looks right: a white room, sea through a big window, pale wood floor, coral player, cyan accents.\n\n**Palette:** white `#f6fafa`, wall shade `#dfe9ea`, sky `#8fd3f4` → `#d8f3fb`, sea `#49b6c9` → `#2f97ad`, floor `#ecd9bd` → `#d9bd96`, UI accent `#2cc6e6`, ink `#20404c`, player coral `#ff7a59`, mint `#bfeee0`, oak `#d9b68a`, maple `#ecd3ac`. Colour never carries meaning alone (ring state also has shape and sound).\n\n**Scene recipe ✔:** paint directly on `r.ctx` first in `draw`, then queue actors. **In `brawler`, +y comes toward the camera** (lower on screen), despite what the card's table suggests: the back wall's base is `r.w(0, -44, 0)[1]`, mats sit near y = 0, floor boards run from y = -44 to y = 90. Shade with `E.mix` bands, keep the window as big as the wall. Character size: 2.1 for one rig, 1.9 for two, 1.5 for four. Scenes: `camera: { zoom: false }` on every fixed camera (the wheel belongs to Step Class).\n\n**Rooms (each needs 3 to 8 props and its own light):** Stillness Deck (open air, sea, wind chimes, ferns), Iron Room (white, mirror, comically small dumbbells, a water cooler, motivational signs: \"You Have Been Doing That Wrong\"), Pier (bunting, benches, gulls), Reception (Tare's mat, brochures), Juice Bar (blender, olives), Bungalow (bed, rail), Raft at dusk (lanterns).\n\n**Lights:** morning ambient about .92, noon lights off, dusk about .62 with warm lamps (`game.lights`). Keep bright scenes bright; a dark look is wrong here. Canvas lighting only: no `enableGPU`, and no WebGPU requirement for the hub.\n\n**Performance is not a goal.** Your brief treats the budget as unlimited, with frame rates and optimization out of scope: add the detail, crowd, particles and lights a scene wants, and don't spend time optimizing.\n\n**Draw these yourself (they make it feel like the source):** Tare; the mannequin joints; Gerald; the Plate; rings; yoga mats; step benches; tiny dumbbells; candle and flame; hoops; thought bubbles; tea tray, olives, glasses, gecko; ski gates, snowman; clothesline, pegs, socks, hamper; water cups; Member Cards. Generic props come from the engine's store: `node engine/tools/asset-find.mjs \"plant pot\"` (✔ benches, succulents, tubs, beds exist; no gym gear), read `engine/docs/ASSETS.md`, cut a set with `engine/tools/asset-set.mjs`. Pigeons and gulls are `E.Blob` with wings.\n\n**Title screen:** the studio, sea, Tare hopping on a mat, the logo with `E.font.title` at scale 3 to 4 in cyan. Keep clear of the corner buttons (top right 110 × 60 CSS px).\n\n---\n\n## 9. Animation recipes (all ✔)\n\nRigs are `E.Humanoid` (`weapon: null`). Player and Regulars `chibi`; instructors `build: 'heroic', limbW: 1.5, torsoW: 2.5, hair: 'bald'` (Alder `'ponytail'`) with every colour key in wood tones. Their ball joints: after `rig.draw`, in the same `r.actor`, for `kneeL kneeR elbowL elbowR shL shR`: `const w = rig.worldOffset(rig.J[k]), p = (rig.lastView || r.view).p(w[0], w[1], w[2]);` then `px.disc` radius 3 and radius 2 in two wood tones at `(ox + p[0], oy + p[1])`.\n\n**Real motion capture, including actual yoga, plays on these rigs.** Cut the small set in section 15. Then:\n\n```js\nconst lib = Mocap.load(window.MOCAP.FITCLIPS);\nfunction makeRig(opts) {\n  const rig = new E.Humanoid(Object.assign({ weapon: null }, opts));\n  Mocap.drive(rig, lib);              // first\n  const base = rig.solvePose;         // then our layer: a hand-posed body, then the wobble\n  rig.wob = [0, 0]; rig.body = null;\n  rig.solvePose = function () {\n    base.call(this);\n    if (this.body) setBody(this, this.body(this));\n    const [ax, ay] = this.wob; if (!ax && !ay) return;\n    const J = this.J, a = ax * .45, b = ay * .3, ca = Math.cos(a), sa = Math.sin(a), cb = Math.cos(b), sb = Math.sin(b);\n    for (const k in J) { if (k === 'bladeDir' || !J[k]) continue; const p = J[k];   // turn every joint about the feet\n      const r2 = p[1] * ca + p[2] * sa, z2 = -p[1] * sa + p[2] * ca, f2 = p[0] * cb + z2 * sb, z3 = -p[0] * sb + z2 * cb;\n      p[0] = f2; p[1] = r2; p[2] = Math.max(z3, 0); }\n  };\n  return rig;\n}\n// each step. A clip turns the rig by its own heading, so aim with tgt minus that turn:\nrig.wob = [p.x, p.y];  rig.mocap = lib.sample(clip, t);   // rig.mocap = null to stop\nrig.update(dt, { x, y, z: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, facing: tgt - (rig.spin || 0) });\n```\n\nFacing: π/2 looks at the camera; 0 is profile. **To hold a pose,** sample inside its window and drift slowly: `t = a + (b - a) * .3 * (.5 + .5 * Math.sin(time * .7))`. Clip motion keeps it alive.\n\n**Pose table** (windows ✔ seen on contact sheets; stork, triangle and dog ✔ seen in the studio):\n\n| Pose | Clip | Window (s) | `tgt` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Stork (one leg, arms wide) | `111_39_part1` | 3.6 to 7.0 | 1.57 |\n| Knee Lift | `111_39_part2` | .5 to 2.4 | 1.57 |\n| Triangle | `111_39_part3` | 2.2 to 5.2 | 1.2 |\n| Warrior (wide stance, arms wide) | `111_39_part3` | 6.6 to 7.6 | 1.57 |\n| Low Lunge | `111_38_part1` | 2.9 to 5.0 | .25 |\n| Down Dog | `111_38_part2` | 2.8 to 5.2 | .25 |\n| Forward Fold | `111_38_part2` | 8.0 to 8.8 | .25 |\n| Low Plank | `111_41_part3` | 3.4 to 6.4 | .25 |\n\nOther clips in the set: `Meditate` (Candle), `Pushup`, `22_14`, `Jumping Jacks`, `Run_Loop`, `Walk_Loop`, `Hop_One_Foot_Loop` (regaining balance), `Dizzy` (stumble), `Get_Up_From_Back` (falls), `Victory`, `Cheering_Two_Hands` (3★), `Stretch_Yawn` (morning), `Sleeping` (Lou, bed), `Greeting` (instructor's bow), `Wave_Hello`, `Waiting_Loop`, `Idle_Subtle` (Regulars). Crossfade with `lib.blend(a, b, k)`, or fade a clip over the rig with `rig.mocapW`.\n\n**Moves with no clip: pose the body yourself.** You set hips, feet, hands; IK does knees and elbows:\n\n```js\nconst { V3 } = E;  // V3.add, V3.mul, V3.norm\nfunction setBody(rig, b) {\n  const o = rig.o, J = rig.J, hipC = b.hip;\n  J.hipC = hipC; J.hipL = V3.add(hipC, [0, -o.hipHalf, 0]); J.hipR = V3.add(hipC, [0, o.hipHalf, 0]);\n  for (const s of [-1, 1]) { const hip = s > 0 ? J.hipR : J.hipL, foot = s > 0 ? b.footR : b.footL,\n      [kn, f2] = E.ik3(hip, foot, o.legUpper, o.legLower, b.knee ? b.knee(s) : [1, s * .3, .1]);\n    J[s > 0 ? 'kneeR' : 'kneeL'] = kn; J[s > 0 ? 'footR' : 'footL'] = f2; }\n  const dir = V3.norm(b.chest || [0, 0, 1]), shC = V3.add(hipC, V3.mul(dir, o.torso)); J.shC = shC;\n  J.shL = V3.add(shC, [0, -o.shoulderHalf, 0]); J.shR = V3.add(shC, [0, o.shoulderHalf, 0]);\n  J.head = V3.add(shC, V3.mul(V3.norm([dir[0], dir[1], dir[2] + .4]), o.neck + o.headR));\n  for (const s of [-1, 1]) { const sh = s > 0 ? J.shR : J.shL, hand = s > 0 ? b.handR(shC, sh) : b.handL(shC, sh),\n      [el, h2] = E.ik3(sh, hand, o.armUpper, o.armLower, [-1, s * .7, -.2]);\n    J[s > 0 ? 'elbowR' : 'elbowL'] = el; J[s > 0 ? 'handR' : 'handL'] = h2; }\n}\nconst add = V3.add;\nconst sideLunge = u => rig => { const o = rig.o, a = Math.abs(u), w = o.footSpread + 5.4;   // feet stay down at full stretch\n  return { hip: [0, u * 3.8, o.hipZ - a * o.hipZ * .4], footL: [.5, -w, 0], footR: [.5, w, 0], knee: s => [1, s * .7, .1],\n    chest: [.28 * a, -u * .1, 1], handL: c => add(c, [4, -.6, -2.6]), handR: c => add(c, [4, .6, -2.6]) }; };\nconst hula = ph => rig => { const o = rig.o, hx = Math.cos(ph) * 2.1, hy = Math.sin(ph) * 2.1;\n  return { hip: [hx, hy, o.hipZ - .5], footL: [.3, -o.footSpread - 1, 0], footR: [.3, o.footSpread + 1, 0], chest: [-hx * .22, -hy * .22, 1],\n    handL: (c, sh) => add(sh, [.4, -6, 1.6 + Math.sin(ph) * .6]), handR: (c, sh) => add(sh, [.4, 6, 1.6 - Math.sin(ph) * .6]) }; };\nconst stepUp = (k, zb = 5) => rig => { const o = rig.o;   // k 0..1: up onto a bench zb high\n  return { hip: [.2 + k * 1.2, k * 1.6, o.hipZ + k * zb * .7], footL: [k > .5 ? 3 : -1, -o.footSpread, k > .85 ? zb : 0], footR: [3, o.footSpread, zb * Math.min(1, k * 2)],\n    chest: [.1, 0, 1], handL: (c, sh) => add(sh, [1 + k * 3, -1.2, -3 + k * 2]), handR: (c, sh) => add(sh, [3 - k * 3, 1.2, -1 - k * 2]) }; };\n```\n\nSet `rig.body = sideLunge(u)` each step (`rig.body = null` to release). Walking on the rope uses the rig's own walk plus arms held out the same way. Faces: `expr: 'smile' | 'wince'` in `rig.update`. Tare and Gerald are hand-drawn with `px` in `r.queue`, with a spring for squash; Tare's portrait is a function passed to `E.Dialog`. Check motion with `node engine/tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Audio (all from code, no files)\n\n**Music is 10% by default.** ✔ `menu: { settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }] }` sets `game.settings.music` and `audio.musicVolume` to .1. Never compensate by raising track volumes.\n\n**Songs:** original, gentle, a bit too pleasant; think hold music in a very clean building. Step notation with `sine`, `triangle`, soft `pulse`, sparse `drums`; use a track's `vol`, `gate`, `vib`, `name`, `on` and `audio.layer` to add parts as you do well. Write about 12: studio, island (morning), island (dusk), yoga pad, iron, step A (100 bpm), step B (120 bpm), jog, ski, tray lounge, laundry pizzicato, festival, ending, plus jingles (star 1/2/3, unlock, day done) via `audio.sting`. Do not reuse the engine's songbook as your soundtrack, and imitate nothing.\n\n**SFX** via `audio.define`: Tare's signature two-note step-on boop, creak, in-ring chime that climbs, stumble, hippo clink, gull, pigeon flurry, flame flick, hoop whirr (pitch follows speed), ski carve (noise), tray clink, olive plop, rope creak, star stamps, menu tick and confirm. The Stork tier 2 balance tone is your own oscillator on `audio.bus('sfx')`.\n\n**Voices: Animalese-style gibberish, a sound per letter, on the voice bus.** `new E.Dialog(game, { voice: (ch, i, talk) => babble(talk.name, ch) })` (`talk.name` is the speaker the current `say` gave). `babble` makes a 60 to 90 ms oscillator (sine or triangle) through a band-pass filter on `audio.ctx`, connected to `audio.bus('voice')`, with pitch and filter from a table by letter (vowels open and longer, consonants short), skipping spaces and punctuation. Each speaker has base pitch, speed, wave and vibrato: Tare high and quick, Birch low and slow, Alder warm, Gertrude quavery, and so on. Guard for `audio.ctx` being null (headless, or before the first input). Add a `voice` slider setting that applies `audio.voiceVolume`. Exercise grunts use the same function.\n\n---\n\n## 11. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\n\n**Rules:** at most 6 choices on a screen; one idea per screen; no tables or data grids anywhere; body text never below font scale 1 (`font: 'tiny'` is banned), key numbers scale 2 to 3; anchor everything to `r.W` / `r.H` with 12 px margins; ✔ judge it from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n**Canvas UI, bright and round.** `E.Menu`'s default is a dark JRPG window: wrong here. Write one **`Pills`** widget (about 70 lines) and use it on every game screen: white rounded pills, cyan focus that grows slightly, soft tick on move. Up/down (or left/right) with `input.repeat`, ✕ or Enter picks, ○ backs out. **Mouse: hover moves focus, a click picks** (`input.pointer()`, `input.clicked()`). `E.Dialog` takes `{ bg: ['#ffffff', '#eaf6f8'], border: '#2cc6e6', color: '#20404c', nameColor: '#14a8c8' }`, but it hard-codes a near-black text shadow that smears on white. **Make this one engine change ✔:** in `class Dialog` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, replace each `shadow: '#05040a'` used for the name, the text and the choices (3 places, around lines 9153 to 9176) with `shadow: this.shadow === undefined ? '#05040a' : this.shadow`, then set `talk.shadow = null`.\n\n**Prompts** come only from one `prompt(action, verb)` helper that draws a chip at bottom right, showing what the player used last. Controller: `input.label(action)` gives ✕ ○ □ △ L1 R1 L2 R2 Options ✔ (the pixel font draws them all). Keyboard and mouse: `input.label(a, 'keyboard') + ' / ' + input.label(a, 'mouse')`, e.g. \"Space / Left click\". Lean's own prompt says \"Left stick\" / \"WASD\" / \"Move the mouse\" by the live source. ✔ `menu: { settings: [{ key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation' }] }` defaults to PlayStation, and the standard Settings → Controller → Button symbols offers Xbox (A B X Y).\n\n**Standard screens stay the engine's** (pause, settings, controls, rebinding, full screen, boot). ✔ Theme and fix them:\n\n```js\nnew E.Shell(game, { theme: { ink: '#20404c', paper: '#f7fbfb', accent: '#14a8c8', muted: '#5f7f8a', danger: '#e0553a', line: '#c8dde2', font: 'system-ui, sans-serif', titleFont: 'system-ui, sans-serif' } });\n// the engine's HTML menus don't move focus on hover. This makes them:\nif (typeof document !== 'undefined') document.addEventListener('pointerover', e => {\n  const b = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('.esh-sh button:not(:disabled), .esh-sh input:not(:disabled)');\n  if (b && e.pointerType === 'mouse') b.focus({ preventScroll: true }); });\n```\n```css\n@media (min-height:700px){.esh-mod{zoom:1.5}} @media (min-height:1000px){.esh-mod{zoom:2}}   /* readable at 10 feet */\n.esh button:focus,.esh input:focus{outline:3px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}\n[data-sys=need]{background:rgba(5,3,12,.35)!important;align-items:flex-end!important}          /* lets attract show through */\n```\n\n**Game settings** (`menu.settings`): `music` .1, `glyphs`, `voice` slider, Gentle Mode, Breath Hold/Toggle, Tare's Tips on/off. `menu.items`: Restart Session, Dev Mode. `menu.quit: 'title'`, autosaving first. `menu.controls` names the actions in plain words and hides the ones a player has no reason to rebind.\n\n**Touch-only devices.** ✔ `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })` shows exactly \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button and no touch controls; the CSS above lets the attract mode show behind it. Attract runs after 10 s as usual (taps produce no actions, so it stays running).\n\n**Comfort:** use `game.shake` / `game.flash`, which follow the settings. Pausing is standard; every activity scene is `pausable: true`.\n\n**About / Credits screen** (from Title): paged, big text, no scrolling wall. Pages: Source Information (every field your brief lists, in its order), Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, Credits (engine; Mesh2Motion and Quaternius, CC0; CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database; asset store sources). `build.mjs` injects your exit-interview JSON into the page as `G.ABOUT`, so screen, file and chat reply cannot disagree. Usage shows \"added on import\" as your brief says.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Attract Mode\n\nAfter **10 s with no input** on the title or any top-level menu (`game.hook('input', ...)`: `anyPressed`, stick, pointer movement). **Any input** returns to the title and swallows the press (`input.consumeAll()`).\n\nFiction: nobody's here, so Tare shows the empty room around. A \"DEMO\" chip, the logo in a corner, \"Press any button\" (by device), and subtitled lines: \"Nobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\" On exit: \"Oh! You're back. I wasn't doing anything.\"\n\n**Playlist, about 15 s each, looping:** Island walk → Body Check → Stork Stand → Sun Flow → Quiet Candle → Squat Rail → Push-Up → Side Lunge → Step Class → Hoop Hips → Coastal Jog → Slalom → Tray Service → Laundry Line → four-mat Class → results with Gerald's coins → Grand Stillness. Each runs the real activity scene with the expert bot filling `intent`, with cheats allowed (no stumbles). It never touches saves or unlocks. Use a Regular's rig as the star.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Dev Mode\n\nReachable from the pause menu (`menu.items`), in every scene, on every device. It closes the pause and docks a canvas panel on the left third **while the game keeps running**, so balance changes are felt live. D-pad up/down moves, left/right adjusts (held accelerates, L1/R1 coarse), ✕ activates, ○ closes. Arrows on keyboard (WASD keeps leaning). Mouse: drag sliders; the pointer over the panel does not lean.\n\n**Live sliders** (all in one `DEV` object with defaults; \"Reset to defaults\" restores it; each shows default vs current):\n- Lean: `k c s A nf`, ring scale, push strength, stumble threshold, mouse reach, nudge rate\n- Scoring: star thresholds, rep tolerance, rhythm window scale, fatigue amount\n- Cardio: hoop band, jog cadence band, jog speed\n- Games: slalom speed and turn, tray gravity and friction, rope instability, gust strength\n- World: time scale (0, .25, .5, 1, 2), minutes multiplier\n\n**Tools:** jump to any scene/activity/tier/day; finish now with N stars; unlock all; +10 minutes; set Spine Age; reset this member; no stumbles; bot plays (poor/average/good/expert); show Plate trace and numbers; frame step; force attract; **Pose Viewer** (pick any clip, scrub, print a pose row for `game/data/poses.js`); log `game.debug.snapshot()` to the console. Hidden in a hub session.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Multiplayer\n\n**Class (local, on its own, 2 to 4).** From the title: join with Start on a free pad or 2 on the keyboard (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`; `game.players[i]` has the same input API; keyboard players get `E.Input.halfKeys`). ✔ Half a keyboard runs out of keys with the full `INPUT` (the step and pace actions get none), so the Class scene sets its own `input`: the moves and menu actions plus `breath`, `catchL`, `catchR` only (left half F G H, right half `. / ,`), and its Step Class reads `lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right']`. Everyone gets a mat, a colour (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) and a pre-made rig, on one fixed screen at size 1.5 with a small Plate under each. Activities: Stork Stand, Quiet Candle, Squat Rail, Step Class (two lanes), Hoop Hips, 35 s each, or \"Surprise me\" (3 rounds). So every class-capable activity takes a list of **contestants** from the start, not one player. Scores are 0 to 1000 (`round(pct × 1000)`). Results: podium with polite titles (Most Still, Best Wobble, Participated). Tare reads them. Empty mats hold Regulars driven by bots, for life, not for score.\n\n**AI Hub session (`ghost` mode, 1 to 4).** Follow the protocol README (`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`); it is short, read it. Outside a session the game is unaffected and `connect()` answers `null`. ✔ This exact shape passed the harness at 1, 2, 3 and 4 players, on the bad network, and with the host leaving.\n\n**The round: \"Morning Class\".** Everyone plays the same 3 events on their own copy, in lockstep, seeing others as translucent seat-coloured ghosts on neighbouring mats (or in the world for Slalom and Jog). About 150 s: each event is 5 s intro + 40 s play + 5 s scores. Deal with `AIHub.rng('deal')`: one from Stork/Candle/Squat/Push-Up, one from Step/Hoop, one from Slalom/Jog.\n\n```js\nconst inSession = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', id: 'GAMEID', res: 'ps1', expand: true, touch: 'never', input: INPUT,\n  autoPause: !inSession, live: inSession, fullscreen: inSession ? false : 'button',\n  menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', items: inSession ? [] : [/* Restart, Dev Mode */], settings: [/* section 11 */] } });\ngame.start({ scenes, scene: inSession ? 'round' : 'title', boot: {/* steps */} });\nif (inSession) (async () => {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n  if (!info) return game.go('title');\n  AIHub.on('card', c => { card = c; });\n  AIHub.on('start', () => {});\n  AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => { /* ghost state */ });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { /* remove that ghost */ });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => report());                  // result() at once if not reported\n  AIHub.on('end', () => { over = true; game.audio.stopMusic(); game.audio.mute(true); game.input.clear(); });\n  await game.booted; AIHub.ready();                     // no key press\n})();\n```\n\n- **Card (yours, `card: true`):** the studio with the players lined up on mats, Tare hopping, the title, each player's name and colour with a ready tick, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left. While `AIHub.time() === -Infinity`: `confirm` or `start` → `AIHub.answer('ready')`, `more` (△) → `AIHub.answer('more')`, clicks on Ready/More too. No menus or choices on the card. Show \"More time\" state from the `card` event (`asked`, `paused`).\n- **Clock:** all event timing comes from `AIHub.time()`, not `game.time`. A frame over 50 ms gives up its time, so a slow machine's game clock lags and would desync. Countdown while negative. Play at ≥ 0. If `info.limitMs` is shorter than the round, shrink the events.\n- **Randomness:** every activity takes its disturbances from `AIHub.rng('e' + eventIndex)` (and a seeded `E.rng` offline). `Math.random` is only for cosmetics like particles and blinks, because copies draw it at different rates.\n- **Ghost data:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', a: eventIndex, l: [x, y], p: phase, w: [wx, wy], s: score }, { reliable: false })` about 10 times a second. Draw only if `a` matches your current event. `r.actor(..., { alpha: .5 })`, name tag in seat colour. Names come from `info.players`, drawn with `E.font` only (never HTML). Limit: 20 messages/s.\n- **Reporting:** `AIHub.progress({ score: total, label: total + ' pts' })` about once a second; at the end `AIHub.result({ score: total, stats: { Steadiness: '84%' }, awards: [{ title: 'Most Still', detail: '...' }] })` once.\n- **In a session:** no title, attract, dev, quit, restart or saved progress. Options opens the settings over the running round (`live`). No chat, emotes or custom names. No other network. Engine already ignores Options while Create is held ✔.\n\n**Head tags (`build.mjs` writes them), in this order ✔:**\n\n```html\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* vendor/session.js, unmodified, first script in head */</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>THE TITLE — a tagline</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"one or two sentences\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#2cc6e6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\"><meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Wii Fit\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Stay steadiest over 3 exercises; most points wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse. Breathe: R2, Space or click\">\n```\n\n---\n\n## 15. Tech and setup\n\n**Stack:** the my-3D2dge full engine (2D views), its `mode7`, `road`, `physics`, `rhythm` modules (all inside `my-3d2dge.js`), `Mocap` and a cut clip set, the hub client. No World3D, no other libraries. **Start from no single kit:** this game mixes genres, so use the full engine with your own page, and read `engine/kits/road.js`, `kart.js`, `rhythm.js`, `pinball.js` (physics) and `sports.js` (joining players) when you build those parts.\n\n**Fetch (✔ every command run from a clean folder; run from the dev folder):**\n\n```sh\ngit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git _src\ngit -C _src sparse-checkout set dist/handoff\ncp -r _src/dist/handoff engine        # then remove _src\nnpm install playwright@1.63.0         # uses the browsers already here. Never `playwright install`, whatever the engine's README says\n\nmkdir -p vendor/clipsrc/tools vendor/clipsrc/src/mocap tests/hub\nB=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main\nH=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/tools/anim-set.mjs $B/tools/anim-set.mjs\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/tools/mocap-lib.mjs $B/tools/mocap-lib.mjs\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/src/mocap/readable.js $B/src/mocap/readable.js    # the tool needs it exactly here\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/readable.js $B/src/mocap/readable.js\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/mocap.js $B/src/mocap/mocap.js\nfor f in src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js src/mocap/sets/cmu.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_111.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_22.js; do curl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/$(basename $f) $B/$f; done\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/session.js $H/session.js\nfor f in harness.html bridge.js round.js; do curl -fsSLo tests/hub/$f $H/$f; done\nnode vendor/clipsrc/tools/anim-set.mjs vendor/clipsrc/mesh2motion.js vendor/clipsrc/cmu.js vendor/clipsrc/CMU_111.js vendor/clipsrc/CMU_22.js \\\n  --clips \"Pushup,Meditate,Jumping Jacks,Sleeping,Victory,Cheering_Two_Hands,Dizzy,Idle_Subtle,Greeting,CMU:Run_Loop,CMU:Walk_Loop,Stretch_Yawn,Get_Up_From_Back,Waiting_Loop,Hop_One_Foot_Loop,Wave_Hello,111_38_part1,111_38_part2,111_39_part1,111_39_part2,111_39_part3,111_41_part3,22_14\" \\\n  --name FITCLIPS --out vendor/fitclips.js --credit \"Mesh2Motion (CC0), Quaternius (CC0), CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses)\"\n# prints 23 clips, about 173 KB. vendor/clipsrc can then go; it is not bundled\n```\n\nMore clips, if you want them: search `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/src/mocap/catalogs/cmu-takes.tsv` (take `NN_xx` lives in `examples/cmu-lib/CMU_NN.js`) and `.../catalogs/mesh2motion.json`.\n\n**Layout:**\n\n```\nengine/        the handoff copy (my-3d2dge.js is the engine; API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md, tools/, kits/, docs/)\nvendor/        readable.js, mocap.js, fitclips.js, session.js\ngame/\n  index.html   dev page: canvas (#screen with CSS width and height 100%, or it draws at 300×150 ✔) and the scripts in order\n  core.js      G namespace, game, INPUT, DEV defaults, state, saves, deep links (#hub, #act/stork/1, #day/3, #ending)\n  balance.js   Balance model, intent sources (devices, bots), Plate\n  rigs.js      makeRig, setBody and moves, Tare, Gerald, joints, cast\n  ui.js        Pills, prompt, Card, Results, DevPanel\n  audio.js     songs, sfx, babble\n  data/        lines.js, poses.js, activities.js, charts.js, courses.js, trays.js, days.js, unlocks.js\n  activities/  hold.js, candle.js, rep.js, step.js, hoop.js, jog.js, slalom.js, tray.js, laundry.js\n  scenes/      title, attract, member, arrival, island, bodycheck, session, evening, games, ending, about, class, round\ntests/run.mjs  the one test command; tests/hub/ the harness\nbuild.mjs      the one build command\n```\n\nPlain scripts on one global `G`, no ES modules (the page must work from `file://`). **Build out by data:** a designer adds a tier, pose, chart, gate course, tray, line or day by editing `game/data/`, with no code change. Add a short `game/data/README.md` saying how.\n\n**Activity registry:**\n\n```js\nG.activity({ id: 'stork', family: 'hold', discipline: 'Stillness', name: 'Stork Stand', view: 'brawler', camera: { zoom: false },\n  class: true, hub: true, tiers: [ {/* numbers */}, {/* numbers */} ], stars: [.35, .65, .90], lines: {/* ... */},\n  setup(ctx) {}, update(dt, ctx) {}, draw(r, ctx) {}, hud(r, ctx) {},\n  result(ctx) { return { pct, detail }; },\n  bot(ctx, skill) { return intent; },\n  ghost(ctx) { return state; }, drawGhost(r, ctx, id, state) {} });\n```\n`ctx`: `{ tier, rng (seeded), contestants: [{ intent, bal, rig, name, color, score, local }], time, done, cheat }`. Every activity becomes its own pausable scene, generated from the entry. Set `game.debug = { snapshot() { return { scene, activity, tier, day, session, pct, stars, minutes, spineAge, lean, source }; } }`: tests and engine tools read it.\n\n**`build.mjs`:** concatenates engine, `vendor/readable.js`, `vendor/mocap.js`, `vendor/fitclips.js`, game files; replaces every `</script` with `<\\/script` in everything it inlines ✔; writes head tags, CSS, the boot markup at the start of `<body>` (copy the `e3-boot` div from `engine/game/index.html`); injects the exit-interview JSON as `G.ABOUT`; writes the single file to the place your brief names (pass it as an argument) and copies it to `tests/hub/game.html`. External CDN is allowed but not needed: inline everything. About 1.5 MB.\n\n**Engine changes:** only the small Dialog shadow patch (section 11) is required. Everything else works through the public API and the wrappers above. Note whatever you change, and why, for your Engine Feedback.\n\n**Traps already found (so you don't lose time on them):**\n1. A custom `input` map replaces the preset (section 3).\n2. `brawler`: +y is toward the camera (section 8).\n3. Mouse movement doesn't change `lastDevice` from `'keyboard'` (section 3).\n4. Default `music` is .5 and `glyphs` 'auto': set both (section 11).\n5. Music at 10% hides the beat: click on the sfx bus (section 4).\n6. HTML menus lack hover focus; the touch notice is 88% opaque (section 11).\n7. `E.Dialog` hard-codes a dark text shadow (section 11). The standard Settings list is long at 10 feet: rely on its scrolling focus and the zoom CSS.\n8. In tests, `game.fadeTime = 0`; `game.go` otherwise delays the new scene .22 s.\n9. A frame past 50 ms gives up its time: browser tests here are software-rendered and slow, so wait on game state, never on the clock.\n10. In Python Playwright use `page.wait_for_timeout`, not `time.sleep` (it freezes the event loop and frames never appear).\n11. `E.store` is shared by id; set `id` on the game, and `E.store.clear()` between test games in one process.\n12. Fixed-camera scenes need `camera: { zoom: false }`, or the wheel zooms instead of stepping.\n","numLines":350,"startLine":236,"totalLines":656}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UnmmVzL2SuzoJhZRySGNb2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
