{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BQpBA3fcCQafg7wfoLPfmb","type":"tool_result","content":"# Building the game out by data\n\nEverything here is plain text and needs no code change.\n\n- **A new line:** add it to any list in `lines.js`. Tone rules are at the top of that file. Keep a box to 2 lines of about 60 characters.\n- **A new tier:** add an object to the activity's `tiers` in `activities.js`. Its numbers are read by the activity's family: `set` is the Lean (k, c, s, A, nf, R, pushV, pushEvery), and `say` replaces the Card's sentence\n- **A new activity from an existing family:** add a row to `activities.js` with `family`, `discipline`, `name`, `room`, `music`, `stars`, `controls`, `say`, `tiers`. Then open it on a day in `days.js` and place its mat i\n- **A new pose:** add a row to `poses.js`: a clip, a window in seconds and a facing. Dev Mode's Pose Viewer prints rows.\n- **A new step chart:** add it to `charts.js`: four lane strings of 16 steps in `parts`, and an `order`. A tier's `chart` names it.\n- **A new slalom course, road or line:** `courses.js`. Gates are x offsets, obstacles are `[x, gate number, kind]`.\n- **A new tray:** add rows to `trays.js`: o olive, G glass, B bumper, # block, ~ gap, K gecko. 12 columns.\n- **A new day:** add a row to `days.js`: `opens` lists activities; `hold`, `catchUp`, `games`, `scene` are the day's beats.\n- **A new unlock:** add a row to `unlocks.js`. Items with `wear` appear on the Bungalow rail.\n- **The island:** `island.js` is 44 x 26 characters. Move a letter and the thing moves.\n5:- Designers: `game/data/README.md` says how to add a tier, pose, chart, course, tray, line or day without touching code.\n/* data/lines.js: every word in the game. Tone rules: short sentences; sincere, polite, a little too personal; never a\n * wink, never a sneer; no body-size talk. A box holds 2 lines of about 60 characters. Add a line to any list: no code. */\n(() => {\n## What this computer cannot settle\nWhether it feels good on a real thumb. A modelled person (reaction delay, device limits) earns stars on every activity through the keyboard, mouse and stick paths, but that is a model. TASK.md lists no controller, no touch device, nobody to listen, no second player, no iPhone and no TV; each was tested through its stand-in.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"fddbce42-abbc-4eb5-8698-2bff67800ebf","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:39:44.767Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Building the game out by data\n\nEverything here is plain text and needs no code change.\n\n- **A new line:** add it to any list in `lines.js`. Tone rules are at the top of that file. Keep a box to 2 lines of about 60 characters.\n- **A new tier:** add an object to the activity's `tiers` in `activities.js`. Its numbers are read by the activity's family: `set` is the Lean (k, c, s, A, nf, R, pushV, pushEvery), and `say` replaces the Card's sentence\n- **A new activity from an existing family:** add a row to `activities.js` with `family`, `discipline`, `name`, `room`, `music`, `stars`, `controls`, `say`, `tiers`. Then open it on a day in `days.js` and place its mat i\n- **A new pose:** add a row to `poses.js`: a clip, a window in seconds and a facing. Dev Mode's Pose Viewer prints rows.\n- **A new step chart:** add it to `charts.js`: four lane strings of 16 steps in `parts`, and an `order`. A tier's `chart` names it.\n- **A new slalom course, road or line:** `courses.js`. Gates are x offsets, obstacles are `[x, gate number, kind]`.\n- **A new tray:** add rows to `trays.js`: o olive, G glass, B bumper, # block, ~ gap, K gecko. 12 columns.\n- **A new day:** add a row to `days.js`: `opens` lists activities; `hold`, `catchUp`, `games`, `scene` are the day's beats.\n- **A new unlock:** add a row to `unlocks.js`. Items with `wear` appear on the Bungalow rail.\n- **The island:** `island.js` is 44 x 26 characters. Move a letter and the thing moves.\n5:- Designers: `game/data/README.md` says how to add a tier, pose, chart, course, tray, line or day without touching code.\n/* data/lines.js: every word in the game. Tone rules: short sentences; sincere, polite, a little too personal; never a\n * wink, never a sneer; no body-size talk. A box holds 2 lines of about 60 characters. Add a line to any list: no code. */\n(() => {\n## What this computer cannot settle\nWhether it feels good on a real thumb. A modelled person (reaction delay, device limits) earns stars on every activity through the keyboard, mouse and stick paths, but that is a model. TASK.md lists no controller, no touch device, nobody to listen, no second player, no iPhone and no TV; each was tested through its stand-in.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BQpBA3fcCQafg7wfoLPfmb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
