{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Z4LHzpr574Se3C2wuKyFT","type":"tool_result","content":"Testing: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n### Sharing this computer\n\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\n28:Testing: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screensh\n54:- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n3:You are building this game alone, from this plan and your brief. Nobody can answer questions, so decide and move on.\n36:1. **One skill, many bodies.** Everything is the Lean (section 3). Learn it once, feel it everywhere.\n39:4. **The daily ritual.** Weigh-in, sessions, recap, bed. Tiny numbers feel huge.\n191:| 4 Tare's Day | Spine Age catches up in one satisfying drop | Tier 2s | Tare's recalibration: a 30 s scene at Reception, Tare on a huge old scale, you press ✕ to read it. \"Three grams. It's the f\n201:**Body Check** (about 50 s): step onto Tare (hop, boop) → Stillness Test, 5 s, small ring → Lean Test, four directions, hold each 1 s → one Silly Question → Reading (\"Today you weigh 11.4 ducks. T\n251:- Idle on the island: \"Are you still there? I can feel you not standing on me.\"\n297:**Draw these yourself (they make it feel like the source):** Tare; the mannequin joints; Gerald; the Plate; rings; yoga mats; step benches; tiny dumbbells; candle and flame; hoops; thought bubbles\n624:| M1 | Lean, intent, devices, bots, Plate; `makeRig`; Tare and voice; studio scene; **Stork Stand** with Card and Results | Feels good on stick, keys and mouse. Bands hold. **Stop and tune here: i\nee36ae60967bdbfc","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"cc3732c3-8df2-4c80-86ef-8fe012f21e01","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:03:27.511Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Testing: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the 