{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjjU2uVo26F1pAZk6Q9c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The \"Nintendo\" option is gone from Settings, and that was the last thing I could act on.** On the final build, `node tests/run.mjs all` gave 2609 passed, 0 failed, and all 36 hand-in checks hold. The file's hash was the same before and after the suite (`242baf78796c7b53…`), and I changed no game code after it.\n\n## The Nintendo fix\n- **What changed:** the game now sets its own Button symbols options through the engine's public settings, so the engine itself is untouched.\n- **How I checked it:** I stepped through the real Controls screen in a browser with a stand-in pad. It offers Auto, Xbox, PlayStation and Positions. A test now covers this too.\n- **What remains:** the word is still in the engine source inside the HTML file, but it's never shown.\n- **Correction to the hook:** the plan bans Wii, Mii and Balance Board by name, not \"Nintendo-era names\". I removed it anyway because it was cheap and has no place on that screen.\n\n## What is not done\nThese are still open, and I don't count them as done:\n- **M1 \"Feels good on stick, keys and mouse\":** nobody has played it by hand.\n- **Section 18's judgment parts:** whether the writing is funny, whether the look stands apart from the source, and whether screens feel uncluttered from 10 feet.\n- **Real hardware:** no controller, iPhone or TV was used, though TASK.md says these are \"never required\".\n\nThe hook is right that \"this needs a person\" is partly my reasoning for feel and humour. The plan sets no measure for \"feels good\", and it says \"Nobody can answer questions\". More testing here wouldn't change that, so I'm stopping rather than rerunning the same checks.\n\n## To finish it\nSomeone needs to play it, starting with these:\n1. Stork Stand on a real controller.\n2. Laundry Line on a keyboard.\n3. Step Class through speakers at the default 10% music.\n4. The whole game on a TV from 10 feet.\n\nThe Source Information and the Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback are unchanged from my earlier reply. They also match `exit-interview.json` and the in-game About screen.\n\nEverything is in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221037__x61bd7e/work/`, and nothing is committed:\n- `WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `WeeTeeter-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-221037/`\n- `PROGRESS.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":754,"cache_read_input_tokens":323276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":754},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e35d4c2a-4185-48d4-8818-8a6b8bcd7047","uuid":"55340e93-34d6-4d1a-a798-5b5d1ec155f2","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:51:56.414Z","request_id":"req_011CgjjU2bdjkhPy9XzY35Va"}
